{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794570180879,"sessionID":"ses_e2b4a243affexa25EPiSDt2Sxc","part":{"partID":"prt_1d4b7d15f001wJX17orDslB1WG","sessionID":"ses_e2b4a243affexa25EPiSDt2Sxc","messageID":"msg_1d4b7af6e00136IppTaQltssNX","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-bcc8ab87f1e82aa3","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"limit":50,"offset":390,"path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-report-pass-1.md"},"output":"Read file specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-report-pass-1.md, lines 390-439\n390: Resource Map Coverage Gate: skipped. `resource-map.md` does not exist in the spec folder, so `resource_map_present` is false in the root config. No lineage emitted a `resource-map.md` either.\n391: \n392: ---\n393: \n394: ## 8. Deferred Items\n395: \n396: - **R2-P1-001 (resolved by the render-hooks-plugin lineage).** The child downgrade still has no per-request input: `SkillAdvisorBriefOptions` carries no `childSession`, so a host that serves a child in-process without setting `AI_SESSION_CHILD` renders a parent brief. The lineage closed it at P1 because the behaviour matches `skill-advisor-hook.md:39`. It reopens as P1 the moment a host is shown dispatching a child in-process.\n397: - **`run` commands that write.** `/doctor:deep-loop` and `/doctor:speckit` are `run` with class `add-only` (`command-attach.ts:80`, `:105`), so they start without asking and add files. The scorer-attach lineage summary said no `run` row writes. Whether `add-only` under `run` is intended belongs in a decision, not a fix.\n398: - **dsh install path.** `/doctor:install` cannot link a dsh runtime because `symlink-manifest.json` has no `dsh` row. Adding one is a feature decision.\n399: - **DR1-P1-001 reach on sandboxed runtimes.** If a supported runtime's sandbox denies a write to one of the allowlisted paths on a default install, the mid-apply fault becomes reachable on a default path and the finding returns to P1. Not verified here.\n400: - **R1-P2-003 reach.** Whether DSH ever emits an operator message with no `source` is not shown by any fixture or store read here.\n401: - **Third no-edit pattern.** `scorer/text.ts:148` holds a copy of the no-edit wording beside `fusion.ts:677`. WG2 records it and leaves it.\n402: \n403: ---\n404: \n405: ## Dimension Expansion Map\n406: \n407: - All four lineages covered all four dimensions (`dimensionCoverage` true for correctness, security, traceability and maintainability in every lineage registry).\n408: - Divergence state is empty in every lineage registry: no pivot started, completed or failed, no audited override, no saturated direction and no remaining frontier recorded.\n409: - Selected directions in the lineages: per-runtime branch logic, mutating-command safety, holdout hygiene and doc-code agreement, plus filesystem write containment in doctor-install.\n410: - This map records breadth only and changes no verdict.\n411: \n412: ---\n413: \n414: ## Search Ledger\n415: \n416: | Lineage | searchCoverage rows | candidateCoverage rows | searchDebt | ruledOutCandidates | cleanSearchProof |\n417: |---|---|---|---|---|---|\n418: | scorer-attach | 6 | 5 | 0 | 14 | 14 |\n419: | render-hooks-plugin | 6 | 5 | 0 | 10 | 10 |\n420: | accuracy-runner | 6 | 5 | 0 | 9 | 9 |\n421: | doctor-install | 6 | 5 | 0 | 5 | 5 |\n422: \n423: hasSearchDebt: false. The graph was unavailable in every lineage, which recorded `graphless_fallback` with direct reads.\n424: \n425: ---\n426: \n427: ## 9. Audit Appendix\n428: \n429: ### Convergence\n430: \n431: Confirmed from each lineage's `deep-review-state.jsonl` (`newFindingsRatio` per iteration) and its `synthesis_complete` event.\n432: \n433: | Lineage | Iterations | Stop reason | Novelty per iteration | Last ratio against 0.10 |\n434: |---|---|---|---|---|\n435: | scorer-attach | 5 | converged | 1.00, 0.33, 0.40, 0.29, 0.00 | below |\n436: | render-hooks-plugin | 5 | maxIterationsReached | 1.00, 1.00, 0.33, 0.23, 0.15 | above |\n437: | accuracy-runner | 5 | maxIterationsReached | 1.00, 1.00, 1.00, 1.00, 0.11 | above |\n438: | doctor-install | 5 | maxIterationsReached | 1.00, 0.27, 0.21, 0.29, 0.125 | above |\n439: \n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 440]","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":true},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-report-pass-1.md, lines 390-439\n390: Resource Map Coverage Gate: skipped. `resource-map.md` does not exist in the spec folder, so `resource_map_present` is false in the root config. No lineage emitted a `resource-map.md` either.\n391: \n392: ---\n393: \n394: ## 8. Deferred Items\n395: \n396: - **R2-P1-001 (resolved by the render-hooks-plugin lineage).** The child downgrade still has no per-request input: `SkillAdvisorBriefOptions` carries no `childSession`, so a host that serves a child in-process without setting `AI_SESSION_CHILD` renders a parent brief. The lineage closed it at P1 because the behaviour matches `skill-advisor-hook.md:39`. It reopens as P1 the moment a host is shown dispatching a child in-process.\n397: - **`run` commands that write.** `/doctor:deep-loop` and `/doctor:speckit` are `run` with class `add-only` (`command-attach.ts:80`, `:105`), so they start without asking and add files. The scorer-attach lineage summary said no `run` row writes. Whether `add-only` under `run` is intended belongs in a decision, not a fix.\n398: - **dsh install path.** `/doctor:install` cannot link a dsh runtime because `symlink-manifest.json` has no `dsh` row. Adding one is a feature decision.\n399: - **DR1-P1-001 reach on sandboxed runtimes.** If a supported runtime's sandbox denies a write to one of the allowlisted paths on a default install, the mid-apply fault becomes reachable on a default path and the finding returns to P1. Not verified here.\n400: - **R1-P2-003 reach.** Whether DSH ever emits an operator message with no `source` is not shown by any fixture or store read here.\n401: - **Third no-edit pattern.** `scorer/text.ts:148` holds a copy of the no-edit wording beside `fusion.ts:677`. WG2 records it and leaves it.\n402: \n403: ---\n404: \n405: ## Dimension Expansion Map\n406: \n407: - All four lineages covered all four dimensions (`dimensionCoverage` true for correctness, security, traceability and maintainability in every lineage registry).\n408: - Divergence state is empty in every lineage registry: no pivot started, completed or failed, no audited override, no saturated direction and no remaining frontier recorded.\n409: - Selected directions in the lineages: per-runtime branch logic, mutating-command safety, holdout hygiene and doc-code agreement, plus filesystem write containment in doctor-install.\n410: - This map records breadth only and changes no verdict.\n411: \n412: ---\n413: \n414: ## Search Ledger\n415: \n416: | Lineage | searchCoverage rows | candidateCoverage rows | searchDebt | ruledOutCandidates | cleanSearchProof |\n417: |---|---|---|---|---|---|\n418: | scorer-attach | 6 | 5 | 0 | 14 | 14 |\n419: | render-hooks-plugin | 6 | 5 | 0 | 10 | 10 |\n420: | accuracy-runner | 6 | 5 | 0 | 9 | 9 |\n421: | doctor-install | 6 | 5 | 0 | 5 | 5 |\n422: \n423: hasSearchDebt: false. The graph was unavailable in every lineage, which recorded `graphless_fallback` with direct reads.\n424: \n425: ---\n426: \n427: ## 9. Audit Appendix\n428: \n429: ### Convergence\n430: \n431: Confirmed from each lineage's `deep-review-state.jsonl` (`newFindingsRatio` per iteration) and its `synthesis_complete` event.\n432: \n433: | Lineage | Iterations | Stop reason | Novelty per iteration | Last ratio against 0.10 |\n434: |---|---|---|---|---|\n435: | scorer-attach | 5 | converged | 1.00, 0.33, 0.40, 0.29, 0.00 | below |\n436: | render-hooks-plugin | 5 | maxIterationsReached | 1.00, 1.00, 0.33, 0.23, 0.15 | above |\n437: | accuracy-runner | 5 | maxIterationsReached | 1.00, 1.00, 1.00, 1.00, 0.11 | above |\n438: | doctor-install | 5 | maxIterationsReached | 1.00, 0.27, 0.21, 0.29, 0.125 | above |\n439: \n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 440]"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"limit\": 50, \"offset\": 390, \"path\": \"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-report-pass-1.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794570178911,"end":1794570180879}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794570180894,"sessionID":"ses_e2b4a243affexa25EPiSDt2Sxc","part":{"partID":"prt_1d4b7d002002lUg44sqHFgOsAn","sessionID":"ses_e2b4a243affexa25EPiSDt2Sxc","messageID":"msg_1d4b7af6e00136IppTaQltssNX","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-ab802800fab57f07","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"limit":80,"offset":218,"path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-report-pass-1.md"},"output":"Read file specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-report-pass-1.md, lines 218-297\n218: ### 3.3 Verified scenarios for the safety-shaped P2 findings\n219: \n220: **R2-P2-001, `command-attach.ts:353`, hub attach ignores a no-edit request. Reach proven.**\n221: \n222: - Input: the prompt \"use sk-doc to create a skill called invoice-parser, do not change anything yet\" with `SPECKIT_COMPILED_ROUTING` unset (`sk-doc` is in `DEFAULT_ON_HUBS`, `compiled-routing-flag.ts:32-40`).\n223: - What happens: `compiled-route.cjs --hub sk-doc` returns `route/single/sk-create-skill` for this and three other no-edit prompts (probe). The full `advisor_recommend` call returns `sk-doc` at 0.8932 with `command: /create:skill` and `policy: start` (probe). The scorer path rules out every command on the same wording (`fusion.ts:887`).\n224: - What should happen: `attachCommand` returns no command when `NO_EDIT_REQUEST` matches.\n225: - Why it stays P2: `start` makes the command's setup ask before writing. `AGENTS.md:68` also says an explicit instruction outranks the policy. A transcript in which a runtime starts the writing steps on such a prompt would raise it to P1.\n226: - Test: `attachCommand('sk-doc', <single sk-create-skill route>, '<the prompt above>')` returns `/create:skill` today and `undefined` after.\n227: \n228: **R1-P2-001, `command-attach.ts:385`, any `/deep:` mention opens the deep-loop gate. Reach narrowed.**\n229: \n230: - Input: a single-mode review route and the prompt \"what did /deep:ai-council decide\".\n231: - What happens: `attachCommand` returns `/deep:review` (probe). On the top recommendation `attachTypedCommand` then replaces it with the typed `/deep:ai-council` (probe of `typedCommandForTop`), which masks the bug in the common case. It still reaches the reader when the `/deep:` text names no tracked command (a typo such as `/deep:reviw`) or when a lower recommendation is enriched (`compiledRouteTopOnly` false, which the prompt hooks never send).\n232: - What should happen: the gate opens only when the typed `/deep:` command equals the command being attached.\n233: - Test: the call above returns `/deep:review` today and `undefined` after, while \"run /deep:review now\" still returns `/deep:review`.\n234: \n235: **R1-P2-002--95282927956e, `command-attach.ts:266`, a file name reads as a typed command.**\n236: \n237: - Input: \"open /create:readme.md and summarise it\" with `sk-doc` on top.\n238: - What happens: `typedCommandIn` returns `/create:readme` and `typedCommandForTop` returns it with `policy: start` (probe), so a request to read a file is offered a writing command.\n239: - What should happen: a `/` or a `.` followed by a word character after the key cancels the match. A sentence-ending period still ends a command.\n240: - Test: `typedCommandIn('see /create:skill.md for details')` returns `/create:skill` today and `undefined` after, while `typedCommandIn('run /create:skill.')` keeps returning `/create:skill`.\n241: \n242: **R1-P2-005, `render.ts:226`, `needsMode` is overridden by a generated row. Latent.**\n243: \n244: - Input: `renderAdvisorBrief` with a top recommendation `{ skill: 'command-create-agent', needsMode: true }` and no `command`.\n245: - What happens: the head reads `use sk-doc → /create:agent (start)` (probe on the built renderer) instead of `(needs a mode)`.\n246: - Reach: none today. `needsMode` is set only for hubs in `MODE_COMMANDS` (`command-attach.ts:394-399`) and no hub id has a command row (probe returned an empty list).\n247: - What should happen: `commandLabel` skips the row backfill when `needsMode` is true.\n248: - Test: the input above prints `/create:agent` today and `(needs a mode)` after.\n249: \n250: **R2-P2-003, `render.ts:233`, the child downgrade reads the wrong row. Latent.**\n251: \n252: - Input: a child session and `{ skill: 'command-speckit-search', command: '/doctor:speckit', policy: 'run' }`. The skill's row is `run` and `read-only`, while `/doctor:speckit` is `run` and `add-only` (`command-attach.ts:105`).\n253: - What happens: the head reads `/doctor:speckit (run)` in the child (probe) where `(parent-named only)` is due.\n254: - Adjustment: the lineage's example (`sk-doc` with `/doctor:overlay apply`) does not reproduce. `sk-doc` has no row and `/doctor:overlay apply` is `ask`, so the pair renders `(parent-named only)`. No producer pairs a command with another command's row today. A recommendation with no row already downgrades (probe).\n255: - Test: the input above prints `(run)` today and `(parent-named only)` after.\n256: \n257: **iter1-P2-offer-reached-unknown, `score-command-transcripts.mjs:1293`, adjusted to a README defect.**\n258: \n259: - Input: an OpenCode run log, whose brief state is always `unknown` (`command-offer.mjs:207-208`), with an offered command on each row.\n260: - What happens: `offerReached` equals `offered`, because the tally counts `briefDelivered !== false`.\n261: - Adjustment: this is the rule the packet specified. Phase 013 task T022 says \"add 1 to a new `offerReached` when `result.offered` and `result.briefDelivered !== false`\". SC-002 pins OpenCode at `offerReached` 3 with `deliveryUnknown` 24. The code is right. The README line at `:111` (\"offers on a turn whose brief arrived\") is wrong.\n262: - Test: no code change, so no failing test. The phase 013 SC-002 summary pin already holds the rule.\n263: \n264: **iter5-P2-credential-hardening-allowlist, `run-command-behaviour.mjs:782`.**\n265: \n266: - Input: an operator shell with `SSH_AUTH_SOCK`, an AWS profile and `NPM_TOKEN` set runs `--runtime claude --set g2 --out <log>` from a prepared arena.\n267: - What happens: `childEnv` copies `process.env` and removes only `GH_TOKEN`, `GITHUB_TOKEN` and `GH_ENTERPRISE_TOKEN` (`:782-789`). The turn runs with `--permission-mode bypassPermissions` (`:126`), so a shell step in it can use the SSH agent, the npm token or the cloud profile.\n268: - What should happen: the child environment is built from an allowlist (path, home, locale, terminal, temp folder and the runtime's own configuration and provider key) or the runner refuses a live arm while such variables are set.\n269: - Why P2: the header's stated threat is a push through this repository's remote. The remote guard at `:986-992` closes it. No fixture prompt asks for network work.\n270: - Test: export `childEnv` and assert `SSH_AUTH_SOCK`, `AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID` and `NPM_TOKEN` are absent from its result. Today they are present.\n271: \n272: **iter2-P2-arena-precondition-unverified, `run-command-behaviour.mjs:986`.**\n273: \n274: - Input: a local checkout after `git remote remove origin`, clean status, with an ignored `.env` and outer git hooks, then a live arm.\n275: - What happens: `remoteNames()` is empty and the dirty check passes, so turns with bypassed permissions run in a tree that never went through `prepare-behaviour-arena.mjs` and its dotenv and hook refusals.\n276: - What should happen: the arena builder writes a marker under the clone's `.git` folder and the first-turn guard refuses a live arm without it (`EXIT_REFUSED`, code `arena_unprepared`).\n277: - Test: a temporary repository with no remote and no marker passes the guard today and returns `arena_unprepared` after.\n278: \n279: ### 3.4 Evidence and tests for the remaining findings\n280: \n281: Each line gives the evidence read in this synthesis and a test that fails today and passes after. Where no such test can exist, the line says so.\n282: \n283: - **DR4-P2-001** `restoreFromBackup` (`:1284-1305`) copies with `path.join` and `copyFileSync` only, while `commandRestore` runs `assertWritable` and the sha256 check (`:1453`, `:1464`). Test: a write hook that damages the backup copy of `AGENTS.md` and drops a line. Today the damaged bytes are restored silently, after the restore stops on the hash mismatch and says so.\n284: - **DR1-P2-003** `foreign` is built at `:587-596` and read only by unit tests (`agents-md-embed.test.cjs:395-974`). Test: a write hook that adds a line above the block. Today apply ends `STATUS=OK`, after it ends `STATUS=FAIL` with a restore.\n285: - **R4-P2-001--d1528b81a2ca** The only `COMMAND_POLICIES` references are its declaration, its emitter (`derive-command-bridges.cjs:1218`) and prose. `advisor-recommend.ts:478` reads `TRACKED_COMMANDS`. A probe found 11 tracked commands missing from `COMMAND_POLICIES`. All 11 are reachable through `MODE_COMMANDS` (`/create:benchmark`, `/create:command`, `/create:diff`, `/create:goal`, `/create:repo-rule`, `/create:skill-parent`, `/create:with-human-voice`, `/deep:ai-council`, `/design:chart`, `/design:diagram` and `/design:extract`). So the scorer lineage's preferred fix (point the attach path at `COMMAND_POLICIES`) would strip the policy from those 11. Delete it instead. Test: `'COMMAND_POLICIES' in await import('../lib/command-attach.js')` is true today and false after, with the deriver's check mode still exiting 0.\n286: - **R4-P2-002--828881666f76** `fusion.ts:750-751` is an `if` with an empty body. Test: none can fail, because removing it changes no output. The scorer suite is the guard.\n287: - **R4-P2-002--de3d8b259d8e** `render.ts:522` compares the literal while `spec-gate-core.mjs:101-106` exports the constant and `isChildSession`. Both accept exactly `'1'` today. Test: a parity test over `'1'`, `'0'`, `'true'` and an empty value. It passes today and guards the drift the finding describes.\n288: - **Q1 (queued item i)** Both files call `renderAdvisorBrief` with no `childSession` option, so `render.ts:522` reads the caller's environment. Under `AI_SESSION_CHILD=1` the built renderer turns `/create:readme (start)` into `(parent-named only)` (probe). The golden file asserts eight `expectedHead` values with `(start)` or `(ask)` plus the ambiguous head. The envelope file asserts one. That makes 10, which matches the coordinator's 10 failures. Without the variable both files pass (12 of 12 and 3 of 3, exit 0). Test: the two files run under `AI_SESSION_CHILD=1` fail today and pass after.\n289: - **iter4-P2-g2-label-grammar-duplication** The runner defines six ids (`run-command-behaviour.mjs:678-698`) and `assertRunnable` accepts any of them (`:724-727`). The scorer rebuilds labels from `STARTED_ROW` (`score-command-transcripts.mjs:929`) and returns `unknown_row` on a miss (`:1156`). All six current ids match. Test: an id added to the shared map outside the regex grammar scores `unknown_row` today and its label after.\n290: - **DR1-P2-001** `copyVerdict` returns `PASS / symlink` at `:709-713` before `expectsAbsent` is read. Probe: `.codex/AGENTS.md -> ../AGENTS.md` reported `PASS symlink`. Test: that tree reports `PASS` today and `FINDING` after.\n291: - **DR1-P2-002** `namesRoot` uses `.some` (`:727`) while the detail at `:731` says every line. Test: a `CLAUDE.md` holding the pointer and one local line reports \"every line names\" today and the corrected wording after.\n292: - **DR3-P2-001** The INFO branch added at `:693-700` is excluded from `failed` and `unmeasured` (`:646-649`). Probe: a tree without `CLAUDE.md` reported `5/6 copies as expected` with the INFO entry inside the five and its `pointer missing` line printed beneath. Test: that tree counts the INFO entry as expected today and separately after.\n293: - **DR5-P2-003** `parseTableRows` drops a row whose width differs (`agents-md-check.cjs:809`) while `addRouterRows` keys rows by rule path with no width check (`agents-md-embed.cjs:329-330`, `:361`). Test: a router row with a literal pipe in its summary reports a missing trigger row today and a malformed row with its line after.\n294: - **DR3-P2-004** `defaultTools` wires four children (`:875-884`) and `spawnSync` runs at `:447`, `:666`, `:768` and `:859`. The README row and the header at `:15` say three. Test: a doc check that the count word equals the `defaultTools` entry count fails today.\n295: - **DR5-P2-001** Probe: `codex-hook-approval-check.cjs --root --json` printed `SKIP no-codex-hooks` and exited 0, while `hook-wiring-check.cjs --root --json` refused with usage. Test: the first call exits 0 today and 2 after.\n296: - **DR5-P2-002** `JSON.stringify(payload).includes(runtime.marker)` at `:123`. Probe: a `.claude/settings.json` whose only prompt entry is `echo hooks/claude/user-prompt-submit.js` printed `ok claude`. Test: an entry that names the marker only in a `description` field reports `ok` today and `hook-missing` after.\n297: - **DR3-P2-002** The absent branch (`codex-hook-approval-check.cjs:171-179`) prints no `repair` line, `doctor-runtime-mirrors.yaml:165-166` promises one and `doctor-setup.yaml:61` routes the state to `/doctor:runtime-mirrors`, whose Codex row only reads. WG6 adds this line and WG7 routes to it: `repair: copy the advisor UserPromptSubmit entry from the Skilled checkout's .codex/hooks.json into <root>/.codex/hooks.json, then approve it with /hooks in a Codex session`. Test: a hooks file without the advisor entry prints no `repair:` today and prints it after.\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 298]","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":true},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-report-pass-1.md, lines 218-297\n218: ### 3.3 Verified scenarios for the safety-shaped P2 findings\n219: \n220: **R2-P2-001, `command-attach.ts:353`, hub attach ignores a no-edit request. Reach proven.**\n221: \n222: - Input: the prompt \"use sk-doc to create a skill called invoice-parser, do not change anything yet\" with `SPECKIT_COMPILED_ROUTING` unset (`sk-doc` is in `DEFAULT_ON_HUBS`, `compiled-routing-flag.ts:32-40`).\n223: - What happens: `compiled-route.cjs --hub sk-doc` returns `route/single/sk-create-skill` for this and three other no-edit prompts (probe). The full `advisor_recommend` call returns `sk-doc` at 0.8932 with `command: /create:skill` and `policy: start` (probe). The scorer path rules out every command on the same wording (`fusion.ts:887`).\n224: - What should happen: `attachCommand` returns no command when `NO_EDIT_REQUEST` matches.\n225: - Why it stays P2: `start` makes the command's setup ask before writing. `AGENTS.md:68` also says an explicit instruction outranks the policy. A transcript in which a runtime starts the writing steps on such a prompt would raise it to P1.\n226: - Test: `attachCommand('sk-doc', <single sk-create-skill route>, '<the prompt above>')` returns `/create:skill` today and `undefined` after.\n227: \n228: **R1-P2-001, `command-attach.ts:385`, any `/deep:` mention opens the deep-loop gate. Reach narrowed.**\n229: \n230: - Input: a single-mode review route and the prompt \"what did /deep:ai-council decide\".\n231: - What happens: `attachCommand` returns `/deep:review` (probe). On the top recommendation `attachTypedCommand` then replaces it with the typed `/deep:ai-council` (probe of `typedCommandForTop`), which masks the bug in the common case. It still reaches the reader when the `/deep:` text names no tracked command (a typo such as `/deep:reviw`) or when a lower recommendation is enriched (`compiledRouteTopOnly` false, which the prompt hooks never send).\n232: - What should happen: the gate opens only when the typed `/deep:` command equals the command being attached.\n233: - Test: the call above returns `/deep:review` today and `undefined` after, while \"run /deep:review now\" still returns `/deep:review`.\n234: \n235: **R1-P2-002--95282927956e, `command-attach.ts:266`, a file name reads as a typed command.**\n236: \n237: - Input: \"open /create:readme.md and summarise it\" with `sk-doc` on top.\n238: - What happens: `typedCommandIn` returns `/create:readme` and `typedCommandForTop` returns it with `policy: start` (probe), so a request to read a file is offered a writing command.\n239: - What should happen: a `/` or a `.` followed by a word character after the key cancels the match. A sentence-ending period still ends a command.\n240: - Test: `typedCommandIn('see /create:skill.md for details')` returns `/create:skill` today and `undefined` after, while `typedCommandIn('run /create:skill.')` keeps returning `/create:skill`.\n241: \n242: **R1-P2-005, `render.ts:226`, `needsMode` is overridden by a generated row. Latent.**\n243: \n244: - Input: `renderAdvisorBrief` with a top recommendation `{ skill: 'command-create-agent', needsMode: true }` and no `command`.\n245: - What happens: the head reads `use sk-doc → /create:agent (start)` (probe on the built renderer) instead of `(needs a mode)`.\n246: - Reach: none today. `needsMode` is set only for hubs in `MODE_COMMANDS` (`command-attach.ts:394-399`) and no hub id has a command row (probe returned an empty list).\n247: - What should happen: `commandLabel` skips the row backfill when `needsMode` is true.\n248: - Test: the input above prints `/create:agent` today and `(needs a mode)` after.\n249: \n250: **R2-P2-003, `render.ts:233`, the child downgrade reads the wrong row. Latent.**\n251: \n252: - Input: a child session and `{ skill: 'command-speckit-search', command: '/doctor:speckit', policy: 'run' }`. The skill's row is `run` and `read-only`, while `/doctor:speckit` is `run` and `add-only` (`command-attach.ts:105`).\n253: - What happens: the head reads `/doctor:speckit (run)` in the child (probe) where `(parent-named only)` is due.\n254: - Adjustment: the lineage's example (`sk-doc` with `/doctor:overlay apply`) does not reproduce. `sk-doc` has no row and `/doctor:overlay apply` is `ask`, so the pair renders `(parent-named only)`. No producer pairs a command with another command's row today. A recommendation with no row already downgrades (probe).\n255: - Test: the input above prints `(run)` today and `(parent-named only)` after.\n256: \n257: **iter1-P2-offer-reached-unknown, `score-command-transcripts.mjs:1293`, adjusted to a README defect.**\n258: \n259: - Input: an OpenCode run log, whose brief state is always `unknown` (`command-offer.mjs:207-208`), with an offered command on each row.\n260: - What happens: `offerReached` equals `offered`, because the tally counts `briefDelivered !== false`.\n261: - Adjustment: this is the rule the packet specified. Phase 013 task T022 says \"add 1 to a new `offerReached` when `result.offered` and `result.briefDelivered !== false`\". SC-002 pins OpenCode at `offerReached` 3 with `deliveryUnknown` 24. The code is right. The README line at `:111` (\"offers on a turn whose brief arrived\") is wrong.\n262: - Test: no code change, so no failing test. The phase 013 SC-002 summary pin already holds the rule.\n263: \n264: **iter5-P2-credential-hardening-allowlist, `run-command-behaviour.mjs:782`.**\n265: \n266: - Input: an operator shell with `SSH_AUTH_SOCK`, an AWS profile and `NPM_TOKEN` set runs `--runtime claude --set g2 --out <log>` from a prepared arena.\n267: - What happens: `childEnv` copies `process.env` and removes only `GH_TOKEN`, `GITHUB_TOKEN` and `GH_ENTERPRISE_TOKEN` (`:782-789`). The turn runs with `--permission-mode bypassPermissions` (`:126`), so a shell step in it can use the SSH agent, the npm token or the cloud profile.\n268: - What should happen: the child environment is built from an allowlist (path, home, locale, terminal, temp folder and the runtime's own configuration and provider key) or the runner refuses a live arm while such variables are set.\n269: - Why P2: the header's stated threat is a push through this repository's remote. The remote guard at `:986-992` closes it. No fixture prompt asks for network work.\n270: - Test: export `childEnv` and assert `SSH_AUTH_SOCK`, `AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID` and `NPM_TOKEN` are absent from its result. Today they are present.\n271: \n272: **iter2-P2-arena-precondition-unverified, `run-command-behaviour.mjs:986`.**\n273: \n274: - Input: a local checkout after `git remote remove origin`, clean status, with an ignored `.env` and outer git hooks, then a live arm.\n275: - What happens: `remoteNames()` is empty and the dirty check passes, so turns with bypassed permissions run in a tree that never went through `prepare-behaviour-arena.mjs` and its dotenv and hook refusals.\n276: - What should happen: the arena builder writes a marker under the clone's `.git` folder and the first-turn guard refuses a live arm without it (`EXIT_REFUSED`, code `arena_unprepared`).\n277: - Test: a temporary repository with no remote and no marker passes the guard today and returns `arena_unprepared` after.\n278: \n279: ### 3.4 Evidence and tests for the remaining findings\n280: \n281: Each line gives the evidence read in this synthesis and a test that fails today and passes after. Where no such test can exist, the line says so.\n282: \n283: - **DR4-P2-001** `restoreFromBackup` (`:1284-1305`) copies with `path.join` and `copyFileSync` only, while `commandRestore` runs `assertWritable` and the sha256 check (`:1453`, `:1464`). Test: a write hook that damages the backup copy of `AGENTS.md` and drops a line. Today the damaged bytes are restored silently, after the restore stops on the hash mismatch and says so.\n284: - **DR1-P2-003** `foreign` is built at `:587-596` and read only by unit tests (`agents-md-embed.test.cjs:395-974`). Test: a write hook that adds a line above the block. Today apply ends `STATUS=OK`, after it ends `STATUS=FAIL` with a restore.\n285: - **R4-P2-001--d1528b81a2ca** The only `COMMAND_POLICIES` references are its declaration, its emitter (`derive-command-bridges.cjs:1218`) and prose. `advisor-recommend.ts:478` reads `TRACKED_COMMANDS`. A probe found 11 tracked commands missing from `COMMAND_POLICIES`. All 11 are reachable through `MODE_COMMANDS` (`/create:benchmark`, `/create:command`, `/create:diff`, `/create:goal`, `/create:repo-rule`, `/create:skill-parent`, `/create:with-human-voice`, `/deep:ai-council`, `/design:chart`, `/design:diagram` and `/design:extract`). So the scorer lineage's preferred fix (point the attach path at `COMMAND_POLICIES`) would strip the policy from those 11. Delete it instead. Test: `'COMMAND_POLICIES' in await import('../lib/command-attach.js')` is true today and false after, with the deriver's check mode still exiting 0.\n286: - **R4-P2-002--828881666f76** `fusion.ts:750-751` is an `if` with an empty body. Test: none can fail, because removing it changes no output. The scorer suite is the guard.\n287: - **R4-P2-002--de3d8b259d8e** `render.ts:522` compares the literal while `spec-gate-core.mjs:101-106` exports the constant and `isChildSession`. Both accept exactly `'1'` today. Test: a parity test over `'1'`, `'0'`, `'true'` and an empty value. It passes today and guards the drift the finding describes.\n288: - **Q1 (queued item i)** Both files call `renderAdvisorBrief` with no `childSession` option, so `render.ts:522` reads the caller's environment. Under `AI_SESSION_CHILD=1` the built renderer turns `/create:readme (start)` into `(parent-named only)` (probe). The golden file asserts eight `expectedHead` values with `(start)` or `(ask)` plus the ambiguous head. The envelope file asserts one. That makes 10, which matches the coordinator's 10 failures. Without the variable both files pass (12 of 12 and 3 of 3, exit 0). Test: the two files run under `AI_SESSION_CHILD=1` fail today and pass after.\n289: - **iter4-P2-g2-label-grammar-duplication** The runner defines six ids (`run-command-behaviour.mjs:678-698`) and `assertRunnable` accepts any of them (`:724-727`). The scorer rebuilds labels from `STARTED_ROW` (`score-command-transcripts.mjs:929`) and returns `unknown_row` on a miss (`:1156`). All six current ids match. Test: an id added to the shared map outside the regex grammar scores `unknown_row` today and its label after.\n290: - **DR1-P2-001** `copyVerdict` returns `PASS / symlink` at `:709-713` before `expectsAbsent` is read. Probe: `.codex/AGENTS.md -> ../AGENTS.md` reported `PASS symlink`. Test: that tree reports `PASS` today and `FINDING` after.\n291: - **DR1-P2-002** `namesRoot` uses `.some` (`:727`) while the detail at `:731` says every line. Test: a `CLAUDE.md` holding the pointer and one local line reports \"every line names\" today and the corrected wording after.\n292: - **DR3-P2-001** The INFO branch added at `:693-700` is excluded from `failed` and `unmeasured` (`:646-649`). Probe: a tree without `CLAUDE.md` reported `5/6 copies as expected` with the INFO entry inside the five and its `pointer missing` line printed beneath. Test: that tree counts the INFO entry as expected today and separately after.\n293: - **DR5-P2-003** `parseTableRows` drops a row whose width differs (`agents-md-check.cjs:809`) while `addRouterRows` keys rows by rule path with no width check (`agents-md-embed.cjs:329-330`, `:361`). Test: a router row with a literal pipe in its summary reports a missing trigger row today and a malformed row with its line after.\n294: - **DR3-P2-004** `defaultTools` wires four children (`:875-884`) and `spawnSync` runs at `:447`, `:666`, `:768` and `:859`. The README row and the header at `:15` say three. Test: a doc check that the count word equals the `defaultTools` entry count fails today.\n295: - **DR5-P2-001** Probe: `codex-hook-approval-check.cjs --root --json` printed `SKIP no-codex-hooks` and exited 0, while `hook-wiring-check.cjs --root --json` refused with usage. Test: the first call exits 0 today and 2 after.\n296: - **DR5-P2-002** `JSON.stringify(payload).includes(runtime.marker)` at `:123`. Probe: a `.claude/settings.json` whose only prompt entry is `echo hooks/claude/user-prompt-submit.js` printed `ok claude`. Test: an entry that names the marker only in a `description` field reports `ok` today and `hook-missing` after.\n297: - **DR3-P2-002** The absent branch (`codex-hook-approval-check.cjs:171-179`) prints no `repair` line, `doctor-runtime-mirrors.yaml:165-166` promises one and `doctor-setup.yaml:61` routes the state to `/doctor:runtime-mirrors`, whose Codex row only reads. WG6 adds this line and WG7 routes to it: `repair: copy the advisor UserPromptSubmit entry from the Skilled checkout's .codex/hooks.json into <root>/.codex/hooks.json, then approve it with /hooks in a Codex session`. Test: a hooks file without the advisor entry prints no `repair:` today and prints it after.\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 298]"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"limit\": 80, \"offset\": 218, \"path\": \"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-report-pass-1.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794570178562,"end":1794570180894}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794570180906,"sessionID":"ses_e2b4a243affexa25EPiSDt2Sxc","part":{"partID":"prt_1d4b7d2b9001d2BLenfuNCpEUO","sessionID":"ses_e2b4a243affexa25EPiSDt2Sxc","messageID":"msg_1d4b7af6e00136IppTaQltssNX","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-ac08f2264805de91","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/render-hooks-plugin; ls -la; echo \"=== strategy head ===\"; head -60 deep-review-strategy.md 2>&1; echo \"=== config ===\"; cat deep-review-config.json 2>&1 | head -50"},"output":"total 272\ndrwx------@ 20 michelkerkmeester  staff    640 Nov 13 07:38 .\ndrwxr-xr-x@ 10 michelkerkmeester  staff    320 Nov 13 12:40 ..\ndrwxr-xr-x@  2 michelkerkmeester  staff     64 Nov 13 07:08 .executor-state\ndrwxr-xr-x@  3 michelkerkmeester  staff     96 Nov 13 07:35 .legacy-projection-watermarks\ndrwxr-xr-x@  4 michelkerkmeester  staff    128 Nov 13 07:37 containment\ndrwx------@  7 michelkerkmeester  staff    224 Nov 13 07:37 deep-review-audit-ledger\n-rw-r--r--@  1 michelkerkmeester  staff   7425 Nov 13 07:35 deep-review-config.json\n-rw-r--r--@  1 michelkerkmeester  staff   7080 Nov 13 07:37 deep-review-dashboard.md\ndrwx------@  7 michelkerkmeester  staff    224 Nov 13 07:37 deep-review-effect-ledger\n-rw-r--r--@  1 michelkerkmeester  staff  27350 Nov 13 07:37 deep-review-findings-registry.json\ndrwx------@  7 michelkerkmeester  staff    224 Nov 13 07:35 deep-review-ledger\n-rw-r--r--@  1 michelkerkmeester  staff  41964 Nov 13 07:35 deep-review-state.jsonl\n-rw-r--r--@  1 michelkerkmeester  staff  23178 Nov 13 07:37 deep-review-strategy.md\ndrwxr-xr-x@  7 michelkerkmeester  staff    224 Nov 13 07:33 deltas\n-rw-r--r--@  1 michelkerkmeester  staff    430 Nov 13 07:08 invocation-metadata.json\ndrwxr-xr-x@  7 michelkerkmeester  staff    224 Nov 13 07:33 iterations\ndrwxr-xr-x@  4 michelkerkmeester  staff    128 Nov 13 07:12 locks-and-fencing-v1\ndrwxr-xr-x@  4 michelkerkmeester  staff    128 Nov 13 07:38 logs\ndrwxr-xr-x@  2 michelkerkmeester  staff     64 Nov 13 07:12 prompts\n-rw-r--r--@  1 michelkerkmeester  staff  19067 Nov 13 07:34 review-report.md\n=== strategy head ===\n---\ntitle: Deep Review Strategy - render-hooks-plugin lineage\ndescription: Session tracking for the render-hooks-plugin fan-out lineage of the command-surfacing review.\nimportance_tier: normal\ncontextType: planning\n---\n\n# Deep Review Strategy - Session Tracking\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\n### Purpose\n\nPersistent brain for the `render-hooks-plugin` fan-out lineage. Records which dimensions remain, what was found (P0/P1/P2), what review approaches worked or failed, and where to focus next.\n\n### Usage\n\n- Read by the executor at every iteration.\n- Updated in place after each iteration; machine-owned blocks stay inside their markers.\n\n---\n\n## 2. TOPIC\n\nReview of command surfacing for the `render-hooks-plugin` area of\n`specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build`.\nScope files are the `render-hooks-plugin` rows of `review/review-scope.txt` (53 files),\nplus shared docs that describe them (`.skilled/agents/orchestrate.md`,\n`.skilled/skills/sk-doc/*`, `system-skill-advisor` root docs).\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:review-dimensions -->\n## 3. REVIEW DIMENSIONS (remaining)\n[All dimensions complete]\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:review-dimensions -->\n## 4. NON-GOALS\n\n- Implementing or editing any reviewed file. The review is observation-only.\n- Re-tuning the advisor scorer, embedders or the command corpus.\n- Reading or reproducing holdout prompt text. Counts only.\n- Reviewing areas owned by the sibling lineages (`scorer-attach`, `accuracy-runner`, `doctor-install`) beyond the shared docs that describe this area's surfaces.\n\n---\n\n## 5. STOP CONDITIONS\n\n- Convergence threshold 0.1 on the weighted new-findings ratio, minimum 2 iterations, stop policy `convergence`.\n- Hard ceiling `maxIterations = 5`.\n- A P0 that would need immediate operator action ends the loop early with `FAIL` and an escalation note.\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:completed-dimensions -->\n## 4. COMPLETED DIMENSIONS\n- [x] correctness\n- [x] security\n- [x] traceability\n- [x] maintainability\n=== config ===\n{\n  \"topic\": \"Review: command surfacing — render-hooks-plugin lineage\",\n  \"sessionId\": \"fanout-render-hooks-plugin-1794550137809-1ecgc7\",\n  \"parentSessionId\": null,\n  \"lineageMode\": \"new\",\n  \"generation\": 1,\n  \"continuedFromRun\": null,\n  \"migrationWindowEndsAt\": \"\",\n  \"maxIterations\": 5,\n  \"convergenceThreshold\": 0.1,\n  \"antiConvergence\": {\n    \"minIterations\": 2,\n    \"convergenceMode\": \"default\",\n    \"stopPolicy\": \"convergence\",\n    \"divergent\": {}\n  },\n  \"stopPolicy\": \"convergence\",\n  \"stuckThreshold\": 2,\n  \"maxDurationMinutes\": 120,\n  \"maxToolCallsPerIteration\": 12,\n  \"maxMinutesPerIteration\": 10,\n  \"progressiveSynthesis\": false,\n  \"specFolder\": \"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build\",\n  \"createdAt\": \"2026-11-13T06:12:00.000Z\",\n  \"status\": \"complete\",\n  \"releaseReadinessState\": \"in-progress\",\n  \"executionMode\": \"auto\",\n  \"executor\": {\n    \"kind\": \"cli-opencode\",\n    \"model\": \"opencode-go/deepseek-v4.1-flash\",\n    \"reasoningEffort\": \"max\",\n    \"serviceTier\": null,\n    \"sandboxMode\": \"danger-full-access\",\n    \"timeoutSeconds\": 900\n  },\n  \"mode\": \"review\",\n  \"reviewTarget\": \"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build\",\n  \"reviewTargetType\": \"spec-folder\",\n  \"reviewDimensions\": [\n    \"correctness\",\n    \"security\",\n    \"traceability\",\n    \"maintainability\"\n  ],\n  \"reviewFocus\": \"Code review of command surfacing. Scope: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-scope.txt lists the changed files, one per line as area TAB path. Revie