{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794570806760,"sessionID":"ses_e2b4a243affexa25EPiSDt2Sxc","part":{"partID":"prt_1d4c161350021mqokp4sVPNdtp","sessionID":"ses_e2b4a243affexa25EPiSDt2Sxc","messageID":"msg_1d4c1559f001BYbhrmTq1GqVd0","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-969c510eca65ff2e","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && ls .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/dsh .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/pi; echo \"=== diagnostic/persist refs ===\"; grep -rn \"persist\\|diagnostic\\|metrics\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/dsh/*.mjs .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/pi/*.mjs 2>/dev/null | head -20; echo \"=== doc context ===\"; sed -n '80,115p' .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook-validation.md"},"output":".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/dsh:\nprompt-advisor.mjs\nREADME.md\n\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/pi:\nprompt-advisor.ts\nREADME.md\n=== diagnostic/persist refs ===\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/dsh/prompt-advisor.mjs:29:// The advisor keys its metrics and outcome records by runtime and drops a label it does not list.\n=== doc context ===\n\n### Step 2: Public Advisor Contract — `advisor_validate`\n\nGoal: verify `advisor_validate` surfaces `workspaceRoot`, `thresholdSemantics`, and prompt-safe `telemetry.outcomes.totals`.\n\n```bash\nnode .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs advisor_validate --json '{\"confirmHeavyRun\":true,\"skillSlug\":null,\"workspaceRoot\":\"<repo-root>\"}' --format json\n```\n\nPass conditions:\n\n- `workspaceRoot` equals the supplied root.\n- `thresholdSemantics` is present and distinguishes **aggregate** (across-corpus) vs **runtime** (per-invocation) semantics.\n- `telemetry.outcomes.totals` contains numeric `accepted`, `corrected`, and `ignored` counts with no raw prompt text anywhere in the payload.\n- Corpus/holdout/parity/safety/latency slices still render (existing contract preserved).\n\n### Step 3: Durable JSONL Diagnostics\n\nGoal: confirm hook diagnostics persist to bounded JSONL sinks under the temp metrics root and that `advisor_validate` can read them back across processes.\n\nEvery hook run writes a prompt-free health record to the diagnostics sink, and `SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG=1` adds the skill label and the error text to each record.\n\n```bash\nexport SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG=1\nls -la \"${TMPDIR:-/tmp}\"/speckit-skill-advisor-metrics/*.jsonl\nhead -3 \"${TMPDIR:-/tmp}\"/speckit-skill-advisor-metrics/*.jsonl\n```\n\nThen drive a prompt through any runtime hook (e.g. the Copilot deterministic smoke in Step 5), and confirm a fresh line appears in the sink and is reflected in the next `advisor_validate` telemetry rollup.\n\nPass condition: sinks are bounded (rotation/truncation visible), contain closed-label fields only, and are picked up by `advisor_validate` telemetry rollups.\n\n### Step 4: OpenCode Plugin CLI Smoke\n\nGoal: confirm the OpenCode plugin's CLI path is wired and routes through the shared render contract.\n\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/dsh:\nprompt-advisor.mjs\nREADME.md\n\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/pi:\nprompt-advisor.ts\nREADME.md\n=== diagnostic/persist refs ===\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/dsh/prompt-advisor.mjs:29:// The advisor keys its metrics and outcome records by runtime and drops a label it does not list.\n=== doc context ===\n\n### Step 2: Public Advisor Contract — `advisor_validate`\n\nGoal: verify `advisor_validate` surfaces `workspaceRoot`, `thresholdSemantics`, and prompt-safe `telemetry.outcomes.totals`.\n\n```bash\nnode .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs advisor_validate --json '{\"confirmHeavyRun\":true,\"skillSlug\":null,\"workspaceRoot\":\"<repo-root>\"}' --format json\n```\n\nPass conditions:\n\n- `workspaceRoot` equals the supplied root.\n- `thresholdSemantics` is present and distinguishes **aggregate** (across-corpus) vs **runtime** (per-invocation) semantics.\n- `telemetry.outcomes.totals` contains numeric `accepted`, `corrected`, and `ignored` counts with no raw prompt text anywhere in the payload.\n- Corpus/holdout/parity/safety/latency slices still render (existing contract preserved).\n\n### Step 3: Durable JSONL Diagnostics\n\nGoal: confirm hook diagnostics persist to bounded JSONL sinks under the temp metrics root and that `advisor_validate` can read them back across processes.\n\nEvery hook run writes a prompt-free health record to the diagnostics sink, and `SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG=1` adds the skill label and the error text to each record.\n\n```bash\nexport SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG=1\nls -la \"${TMPDIR:-/tmp}\"/speckit-skill-advisor-metrics/*.jsonl\nhead -3 \"${TMPDIR:-/tmp}\"/speckit-skill-advisor-metrics/*.jsonl\n```\n\nThen drive a prompt through any runtime hook (e.g. the Copilot deterministic smoke in Step 5), and confirm a fresh line appears in the sink and is reflected in the next `advisor_validate` telemetry rollup.\n\nPass condition: sinks are bounded (rotation/truncation visible), contain closed-label fields only, and are picked up by `advisor_validate` telemetry rollups.\n\n### Step 4: OpenCode Plugin CLI Smoke\n\nGoal: confirm the OpenCode plugin's CLI path is wired and routes through the shared render contract.\n\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && ls .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/dsh .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/pi; echo \\\"=== diagnostic/persist refs ===\\\"; grep -rn \\\"persist\\\\|diagnostic\\\\|metrics\\\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/dsh/*.mjs .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/pi/*.mjs 2>/dev/null | head -20; echo \\\"=== doc context ===\\\"; sed -n '80,115p' .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook-validation.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794570805557,"end":1794570806760}}}}
