{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794570960343,"sessionID":"ses_e2b4a243affexa25EPiSDt2Sxc","part":{"partID":"prt_1d4c3b454002POaULzOgqi3QSt","sessionID":"ses_e2b4a243affexa25EPiSDt2Sxc","messageID":"msg_1d4c3a63e001eiHjrphypx3rT4","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-b802e0bb42aa80d3","tool":"edit","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"newString":"- Comparing duplicate command strings in `COMMAND_ROWS` before trusting the new class lookup avoided a false finding (iteration 1): the only two duplicates carry the same class.\n- Measuring the CLI with and without the new compiled-route request settled a latency suspicion with numbers (88-98 ms vs 134-160 ms warm) instead of inference (iteration 2).\n\n---\n\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\n\n- Treating the new stderr cap as a pure win missed its cost until the test itself showed the busy marker disappearing past the cap (iteration 2). Reading the test's own assertion is what surfaced finding 2.","oldString":"- Comparing duplicate command strings in `COMMAND_ROWS` before trusting the new class lookup avoided a false finding (iteration 1): the only two duplicates carry the same class.\n\n---\n\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\n\n- Nothing failed yet. The remaining pass-one fixes (session readers, `subprocess.ts`, docs) are scheduled for iterations 2-4.","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/render-hooks-plugin-2/deep-review-strategy.md"},"output":"Edited specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/render-hooks-plugin-2/deep-review-strategy.md (1 replacement)","title":"edit","metadata":{"metadata":{"files":[{"file":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/render-hooks-plugin-2/deep-review-strategy.md","patch":"Index: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/render-hooks-plugin-2/deep-review-strategy.md\n===================================================================\n--- specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/render-hooks-plugin-2/deep-review-strategy.md\n+++ specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/render-hooks-plugin-2/deep-review-strategy.md\n@@ -83,14 +83,15 @@\n ## 8. WHAT WORKED\n \n - Reading the committed diff of each pass-one fix against its owning test, rather than the old report text, showed all three `render.ts` fixes intact in one pass (iteration 1). The deleted 35-entry `DOCTOR_COMMAND_STRINGS` map could have silently dropped a doctor bridge; a key-set comparison against `COMMAND_ROWS` proved it did not.\n - Comparing duplicate command strings in `COMMAND_ROWS` before trusting the new class lookup avoided a false finding (iteration 1): the only two duplicates carry the same class.\n+- Measuring the CLI with and without the new compiled-route request settled a latency suspicion with numbers (88-98 ms vs 134-160 ms warm) instead of inference (iteration 2).\n \n ---\n \n ## 9. WHAT FAILED\n \n-- Nothing failed yet. The remaining pass-one fixes (session readers, `subprocess.ts`, docs) are scheduled for iterations 2-4.\n+- Treating the new stderr cap as a pure win missed its cost until the test itself showed the busy marker disappearing past the cap (iteration 2). Reading the test's own assertion is what surfaced finding 2.\n \n ---\n \n <!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n","status":"modified","additions":2,"deletions":1}],"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Edited specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/render-hooks-plugin-2/deep-review-strategy.md (1 replacement)"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"newString\": \"- Comparing duplicate command strings in `COMMAND_ROWS` before trusting the new class lookup avoided a false finding (iteration 1): the only two duplicates carry the same class.\\n- Measuring the CLI with and without the new compiled-route request settled a latency suspicion with numbers (88-98 ms vs 134-160 ms warm) instead of inference (iteration 2).\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\\n\\n- Treating the new stderr cap as a pure win missed its cost until the test itself showed the busy marker disappearing past the cap (iteration 2). Reading the test's own assertion is what surfaced finding 2.\", \"oldString\": \"- Comparing duplicate command strings in `COMMAND_ROWS` before trusting the new class lookup avoided a false finding (iteration 1): the only two duplicates carry the same class.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\\n\\n- Nothing failed yet. The remaining pass-one fixes (session readers, `subprocess.ts`, docs) are scheduled for iterations 2-4.\", \"path\": \"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/render-hooks-plugin-2/deep-review-strategy.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794570957908,"end":1794570960343}}}}
