{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794571143015,"sessionID":"ses_e2b4a243affexa25EPiSDt2Sxc","part":{"partID":"prt_1d4c63716002zDW5Ad06Z0z966","sessionID":"ses_e2b4a243affexa25EPiSDt2Sxc","messageID":"msg_1d4c60cfb0018RGEgQ5vih4u52","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-a83a9488e53ff515","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Review Iteration 003\n\n## Dispatcher\n\n- Mode: review (fan-out lineage `render-hooks-plugin-2`, pass two)\n- Session: `fanout-render-hooks-plugin-2-1794570021136-noekp0`, generation 1, lineage mode `new`\n- Review target: `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build`\n- Area: `render-hooks-plugin` — the shared session readers and their tests\n- Operator review focus addressed this iteration: pass-one fix verification for the session-reader cluster (`R1-P2-002--fabc628596e7`, `R1-P2-003`, `R1-P2-004`, `R4-P2-001--09ff48e9a0b9`) and \"behaviour on claude, codex, opencode, pi, devin and dsh\" through the reader layer.\n- Budget profile: `verify` (11 analysis actions)\n\n## Files Reviewed\n\n- `.skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/claude.mjs:158-250` — attachment extraction, containment-resolved read, injected list\n- `.skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/devin.mjs:182-250`, `:312-450` — chain injection, database projection return shape, transcript fallback\n- `.skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/dsh.mjs:238-250`, `:280-335` — injected notices, contained read, decoder locator\n- `.skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/pi.mjs:160-290` — custom-message extraction, pre-read containment, guard re-resolution\n- `.skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/index.mjs:100-150` — `readSession` vs `loadSession` envelopes\n- `.skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/README.md:15-50` — contained-open rule, `injected` contract, failure codes\n- `.skilled/hooks/shared/tests/session-readers/devin.test.mjs:60-135` — damaged-database fallback, injected continuation\n- `.skilled/hooks/shared/tests/session-readers/dsh.test.mjs:40-95` — injected notice, unsourced event fail-closed\n- `.skilled/hooks/shared/tests/session-readers/pi.test.mjs:112-171` — custom message, linked-outside refusal\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/hooks/advisor-runtime-list-parity.vitest.ts:120-140` — capabilities parity\n- Git diff `35c3188681..HEAD` for all files above\n\n## Findings - New\n\n### P0 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n### P1 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n### P2 Findings\n\nNone. The four reader fixes hold and the new `injected` list is documented where the two envelopes diverge.\n\n## Pass-One Fix Verification\n\n- **R1-P2-002--fabc628596e7 (open `containment.path`, not the caller path) — fix holds in all four readers.** `claude.mjs:217` reads `storePath` (the `resolveInside` result assigned at `:214`); `devin.mjs:354` reads `storePath` inside `loadTranscript`; `dsh.mjs:313` reads `storePath` while passing the locator name only to the decoder; `pi.mjs:233-262` resolves before the header read and opens `guard.path`. Each call site is the only read of the session bytes in its reader.\n- **R1-P2-004 (`devin.mjs:395`, database failure must fall through to the transcript) — fix holds.** `transcriptFallback` at `devin.mjs:397-405` is used by the open failure (`:415`), the chain failure (`:431`) and the catch-all (`:449`). `tests/session-readers/devin.test.mjs:66-76` overwrites `sessions.db` with `not a database` and asserts the transcript wins with `locatorKind: 'transcript_file'`. The pass-one caveat (a transcript that also fails keeps `store_unreadable`) is exactly the README sentence added at `README.md:48`.\n- **R1-P2-003 (`dsh.mjs:195`, an unsourced operator message stays fail-closed) — fix holds.** `injectedFromEvents` at `dsh.mjs:241-257` classifies every `user/message` whose `source.kind` is not `OPERATOR_SOURCE` as injected, with `source: 'unknown'` when no source names one. `tests/session-readers/dsh.test.mjs:64-84` pins it: the unsourced text appears in `injected` as `unknown` and in no record. The reader README states the rule at `README.md:35`.\n- **R4-P2-001--09ff48e9a0b9 (`index.mjs:28`, capabilities not in the parity test) — fix holds.** `tests/hooks/advisor-runtime-list-parity.vitest.ts:134` compares `Object.keys(capabilities).sort()` with `ADVISOR_RUNTIME_VALUES`. The test passed.\n- Test run: `env -u AI_SESSION_CHILD npx vitest run tests/hooks/advisor-runtime-list-parity.vitest.ts` -> 1 file, 1 test passed, exit 0. The reader suites are `node:test` files whose run is recorded in iteration 010 of the pass-one lineage; this pass read the changed cases line by line instead of re-running the whole suite.\n\n## Traceability Checks\n\n| Protocol | Level | Status | Notes |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `spec_code` | core | partial | The `injected` contract matches README; the two envelopes (`readSession` projected, `loadSession` raw) are documented at `README.md:31`. |\n| `checklist_evidence` | core | notApplicable | No checklist row governs the reader layer. |\n| `skill_agent` | overlay | notApplicable | No agent definition in this area. |\n| `agent_cross_runtime` | overlay | pass | Claude, Pi, Devin and DSH readers each expose `injected`; Codex and OpenCode readers are unchanged and the dispatcher forwards the field only when a reader returns it (`index.mjs:138-143`). |\n| `feature_catalog_code` | overlay | deferred | Reader behavior is described in `hooks-and-plugin/claude-hook.md`, reviewed in iteration 4. |\n| `playbook_capability` | overlay | notApplicable | No playbook surface in this iteration. |\n\n## Integration Evidence\n\n- Dispatcher surface: `.skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/index.mjs` exports `readSession` (projected) and `loadSession` (raw); the raw path is the only one that carries `injected` (`:135-145`), and the README names that split so a caller cannot expect it from `readSession`.\n- Consumer named: the callers that check `capabilities` before offering history are the compaction hooks and the lookup CLI (`index.mjs:1-8`), not the dispatcher.\n- Containment helper named: `resolveInside`/`guardSessionPath` in `.skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/identity.mjs:93-138`.\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n- **Scope-marker accuracy.** `review/review-scope-2.txt` marks 30 of this area's 59 files `no` for \"changed since pass one\" although `git diff 35c3188681..HEAD` names every one of them; the marks therefore mean \"unchanged since pass one closed\", not \"unchanged in the window\". The 29 `yes` files were reviewed line by line and the `no` files were read where a `yes` file depends on them (`index.mjs` envelopes, `claude.mjs` read path, `identity.mjs` guards). No code defect follows; recorded so the merged report does not claim the `no` rows were skipped.\n- **DSH decoder takes the locator name.** `decodeSessionLog(readFileSync(storePath), logPath)` picks zstd by the locator extension while reading the resolved target. A file-level link whose name and target extensions differ would decode wrongly, but the pre-fix code read the same bytes through the link and chose the same decoder, so the fix neither introduced nor widened it. Recorded under Ruled Out.\n- **Devin `session_ambiguous` collapse.** When the database fails and the transcript path is ambiguous, `transcriptFallback` reports `store_unreadable` rather than `session_ambiguous`. The README sentence makes that the stated contract for the Devin fallback, and the dominant condition is the failed database, so this is not a finding.\n\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\n\n- No reader opens a path before its containment check: each read site uses a value returned by `resolveInside` or `guardSessionPath` (`claude.mjs:217`, `devin.mjs:354`, `dsh.mjs:313`, `pi.mjs:233`).\n- `injected` is never folded into `records`: the DSH unsourced event and the Pi custom message are asserted absent from records (`dsh.test.mjs:78-83`, `pi.test.mjs:134-136`).\n- `readSession` still returns one envelope and never throws; `loadSession` forwards `injected` only when the reader returned an array (`index.mjs:138-143`).\n- The capability table marks `cursor` gated with a reason and the parity test keeps the runtime list aligned (`index.mjs:24-66`, parity test `:134`).\n\n## Ruled Out\n\n- **The DSH decoder/reader path split is a new defect.** `decodeSessionLog` selected its format from the locator name before this change too; the fix changed only which path's bytes are read. A mismatched link extension fails identically on the base commit.\n- **`readSession` dropping `injected` hides a fix.** The README states the split (`README.md:31`), and the two consumers that need injection text use the raw `loadSession` path. No caller is left guessing.\n- **Devin's fallback masks `session_not_found`.** A missing transcript after a damaged database is the `store_unreadable` case the README names; the database failure is the primary condition.\n\n## Next Focus\n\n- Dimension: traceability\n- Focus area: the `yes` docs in this area — `feature-catalog/cli-surface/advisor-recommend.md`, `feature-catalog/hooks-and-plugin/claude-hook.md`, `hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md`, `.opencode/plugins/README.md`, and the shared `ARCHITECTURE.md`/`README.md` where they describe the command brief.\n- Reason: the reader layer is clean; the remaining pass-one doc findings (`R3-P2-002--ecbea1260371`, `Q2`) and the command-surfacing documentation exist only as prose and must be checked against the code read in iterations 1-3.\n- Rotation status: dimension 3 of 4.\n- Blocked/productive carry-forward: none.\n- Required evidence: each doc line against the code line it describes, plus the pass-one table rows for this area.\n\nReview verdict: PASS\n","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/render-hooks-plugin-2/iterations/iteration-003.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/render-hooks-plugin-2/iterations/iteration-003.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/render-hooks-plugin-2/iterations/iteration-003.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\": \"# Review Iteration 003\\n\\n## Dispatcher\\n\\n- Mode: review (fan-out lineage `render-hooks-plugin-2`, pass two)\\n- Session: `fanout-render-hooks-plugin-2-1794570021136-noekp0`, generation 1, lineage mode `new`\\n- Review target: `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build`\\n- Area: `render-hooks-plugin` — the shared session readers and their tests\\n- Operator review focus addressed this iteration: pass-one fix verification for the session-reader cluster (`R1-P2-002--fabc628596e7`, `R1-P2-003`, `R1-P2-004`, `R4-P2-001--09ff48e9a0b9`) and \\\"behaviour on claude, codex, opencode, pi, devin and dsh\\\" through the reader layer.\\n- Budget profile: `verify` (11 analysis actions)\\n\\n## Files Reviewed\\n\\n- `.skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/claude.mjs:158-250` — attachment extraction, containment-resolved read, injected list\\n- `.skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/devin.mjs:182-250`, `:312-450` — chain injection, database projection return shape, transcript fallback\\n- `.skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/dsh.mjs:238-250`, `:280-335` — injected notices, contained read, decoder locator\\n- `.skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/pi.mjs:160-290` — custom-message extraction, pre-read containment, guard re-resolution\\n- `.skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/index.mjs:100-150` — `readSession` vs `loadSession` envelopes\\n- `.skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/README.md:15-50` — contained-open rule, `injected` contract, failure codes\\n- `.skilled/hooks/shared/tests/session-readers/devin.test.mjs:60-135` — damaged-database fallback, injected continuation\\n- `.skilled/hooks/shared/tests/session-readers/dsh.test.mjs:40-95` — injected notice, unsourced event fail-closed\\n- `.skilled/hooks/shared/tests/session-readers/pi.test.mjs:112-171` — custom message, linked-outside refusal\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/hooks/advisor-runtime-list-parity.vitest.ts:120-140` — capabilities parity\\n- Git diff `35c3188681..HEAD` for all files above\\n\\n## Findings - New\\n\\n### P0 Findings\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n### P1 Findings\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n### P2 Findings\\n\\nNone. The four reader fixes hold and the new `injected` list is documented where the two envelopes diverge.\\n\\n## Pass-One Fix Verification\\n\\n- **R1-P2-002--fabc628596e7 (open `containment.path`, not the caller path) — fix holds in all four readers.** `claude.mjs:217` reads `storePath` (the `resolveInside` result assigned at `:214`); `devin.mjs:354` reads `storePath` inside `loadTranscript`; `dsh.mjs:313` reads `storePath` while passing the locator name only to the decoder; `pi.mjs:233-262` resolves before the header read and opens `guard.path`. Each call site is the only read of the session bytes in its reader.\\n- **R1-P2-004 (`devin.mjs:395`, database failure must fall through to the transcript) — fix holds.** `transcriptFallback` at `devin.mjs:397-405` is used by the open failure (`:415`), the chain failure (`:431`) and the catch-all (`:449`). `tests/session-readers/devin.test.mjs:66-76` overwrites `sessions.db` with `not a database` and asserts the transcript wins with `locatorKind: 'transcript_file'`. The pass-one caveat (a transcript that also fails keeps `store_unreadable`) is exactly the README sentence added at `README.md:48`.\\n- **R1-P2-003 (`dsh.mjs:195`, an unsourced operator message stays fail-closed) — fix holds.** `injectedFromEvents` at `dsh.mjs:241-257` classifies every `user/message` whose `source.kind` is not `OPERATOR_SOURCE` as injected, with `source: 'unknown'` when no source names one. `tests/session-readers/dsh.test.mjs:64-84` pins it: the unsourced text appears in `injected` as `unknown` and in no record. The reader README states the rule at `README.md:35`.\\n- **R4-P2-001--09ff48e9a0b9 (`index.mjs:28`, capabilities not in the parity test) — fix holds.** `tests/hooks/advisor-runtime-list-parity.vitest.ts:134` compares `Object.keys(capabilities).sort()` with `ADVISOR_RUNTIME_VALUES`. The test passed.\\n- Test run: `env -u AI_SESSION_CHILD npx vitest run tests/hooks/advisor-runtime-list-parity.vitest.ts` -> 1 file, 1 test passed, exit 0. The reader suites are `node:test` files whose run is recorded in iteration 010 of the pass-one lineage; this pass read the changed cases line by line instead of re-running the whole suite.\\n\\n## Traceability Checks\\n\\n| Protocol | Level | Status | Notes |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| `spec_code` | core | partial | The `injected` contract matches README; the two envelopes (`readSession` projected, `loadSession` raw) are documented at `README.md:31`. |\\n| `checklist_evidence` | core | notApplicable | No checklist row governs the reader layer. |\\n| `skill_agent` | overlay | notApplicable | No agent definition in this area. |\\n| `agent_cross_runtime` | overlay | pass | Claude, Pi, Devin and DSH readers each expose `injected`; Codex and OpenCode readers are unchanged and the dispatcher forwards the field only when a reader returns it (`index.mjs:138-143`). |\\n| `feature_catalog_code` | overlay | deferred | Reader behavior is described in `hooks-and-plugin/claude-hook.md`, reviewed in iteration 4. |\\n| `playbook_capability` | overlay | notApplicable | No playbook surface in this iteration. |\\n\\n## Integration Evidence\\n\\n- Dispatcher surface: `.skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/index.mjs` exports `readSession` (projected) and `loadSession` (raw); the raw path is the only one that carries `injected` (`:135-145`), and the README names that split so a caller cannot expect it from `readSession`.\\n- Consumer named: the callers that check `capabilities` before offering history are the compaction hooks and the lookup CLI (`index.mjs:1-8`), not the dispatcher.\\n- Containment helper named: `resolveInside`/`guardSessionPath` in `.skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/identity.mjs:93-138`.\\n\\n## Edge Cases\\n\\n- **Scope-marker accuracy.** `review/review-scope-2.txt` marks 30 of this area's 59 files `no` for \\\"changed since pass one\\\" although `git diff 35c3188681..HEAD` names every one of them; the marks therefore mean \\\"unchanged since pass one closed\\\", not \\\"unchanged in the window\\\". The 29 `yes` files were reviewed line by line and the `no` files were read where a `yes` file depends on them (`index.mjs` envelopes, `claude.mjs` read path, `identity.mjs` guards). No code defect follows; recorded so the merged report does not claim the `no` rows were skipped.\\n- **DSH decoder takes the locator name.** `decodeSessionLog(readFileSync(storePath), logPath)` picks zstd by the locator extension while reading the resolved target. A file-level link whose name and target extensions differ would decode wrongly, but the pre-fix code read the same bytes through the link and chose the same decoder, so the fix neither introduced nor widened it. Recorded under Ruled Out.\\n- **Devin `session_ambiguous` collapse.** When the database fails and the transcript path is ambiguous, `transcriptFallback` reports `store_unreadable` rather than `session_ambiguous`. The README sentence makes that the stated contract for the Devin fallback, and the dominant condition is the failed database, so this is not a finding.\\n\\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\\n\\n- No reader opens a path before its containment check: each read site uses a value returned by `resolveInside` or `guardSessionPath` (`claude.mjs:217`, `devin.mjs:354`, `dsh.mjs:313`, `pi.mjs:233`).\\n- `injected` is never folded into `records`: the DSH unsourced event and the Pi custom message are asserted absent from records (`dsh.test.mjs:78-83`, `pi.test.mjs:134-136`).\\n- `readSession` still returns one envelope and never throws; `loadSession` forwards `injected` only when the reader returned an array (`index.mjs:138-143`).\\n- The capability table marks `cursor` gated with a reason and the parity test keeps the runtime list aligned (`index.mjs:24-66`, parity test `:134`).\\n\\n## Ruled Out\\n\\n- **The DSH decoder/reader path split is a new defect.** `decodeSessionLog` selected its format from the locator name before this change too; the fix changed only which path's bytes are read. A mismatched link extension fails identically on the base commit.\\n- **`readSession` dropping `injected` hides a fix.** The README states the split (`README.md:31`), and the two consumers that need injection text use the raw `loadSession` path. No caller is left guessing.\\n- **Devin's fallback masks `session_not_found`.** A missing transcript after a damaged database is the `store_unreadable` case the README names; the database failure is the primary condition.\\n\\n## Next Focus\\n\\n- Dimension: traceability\\n- Focus area: the `yes` docs in this area — `feature-catalog/cli-surface/advisor-recommend.md`, `feature-catalog/hooks-and-plugin/claude-hook.md`, `hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md`, `.opencode/plugins/README.md`, and the shared `ARCHITECTURE.md`/`README.md` where they describe the command brief.\\n- Reason: the reader layer is clean; the remaining pass-one doc findings (`R3-P2-002--ecbea1260371`, `Q2`) and the command-surfacing documentation exist only as prose and must be checked against the code read in iterations 1-3.\\n- Rotation status: dimension 3 of 4.\\n- Blocked/productive carry-forward: none.\\n- Required evidence: each doc line against the code line it describes, plus the pass-one table rows for this area.\\n\\nReview verdict: PASS\\n\", \"path\": \"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/render-hooks-plugin-2/iterations/iteration-003.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794571122454,"end":1794571143015}}}}
