{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794571318739,"sessionID":"ses_e2b4a243affexa25EPiSDt2Sxc","part":{"partID":"prt_1d4c92c19001DCYQdDJD8TgPm5","sessionID":"ses_e2b4a243affexa25EPiSDt2Sxc","messageID":"msg_1d4c91428001JMnTjszuvOXl0c","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-9695c77bf29b7a55","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && grep -n \"includeCompiledRoute: z.boolean\\|compiledRouteTopOnly: z.boolean\\|command: z.string().min(1).optional()\\|const options = patternString\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts | head; echo \"=== command field in recommendation schema ===\"; grep -n \"command:\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts | head; echo \"=== handler skips ===\"; grep -n \"includeCompiledRoute === false\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/handlers/advisor-recommend.ts; echo \"=== doc claims ===\"; grep -n \"advisor-tool-schemas.ts:287\\|advisor-tool-schemas.ts:290\\|advisor-tool-schemas.ts:310\\|advisor-recommend.ts:563-565\\|advisor-recommend.ts:632-634\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/cli-surface/advisor-recommend.md"},"output":"295:    includeCompiledRoute: z.boolean().optional(),\n298:    compiledRouteTopOnly: z.boolean().optional(),\n321:  command: z.string().min(1).optional(),\n=== command field in recommendation schema ===\n321:  command: z.string().min(1).optional(),\n=== handler skips ===\n630:      input.options?.includeCompiledRoute === false\n705:    input.options?.includeCompiledRoute === false\n=== doc claims ===\n33:When a recommendation gets a `compiledRoute`, `enrichCompiledRoutes()` also asks `attachCommand()` in `lib/command-attach.ts` for a slash command and sets the optional `command` field when one comes back (`schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts:310`, `z.string().min(1).optional()`). `attachCommand()` names a command only for a `route` decision with `selectionKind: 'single'` and exactly one target, and only when the generated `MODE_COMMANDS` table maps that hub and `workflowMode` to a command. A bundle, a multi-target route or a mode with no command leaves `command` off. For `system-deep-loop` the prompt must type the same command or hold a phrase from `DEPTH_WORDING`, so a prompt that only names a topic such as research or review gets no deep-loop command. A prompt that matches `NO_EDIT_REQUEST` gets no command from any hub, because a reader who rules out a change is never handed work that writes.\n35:The request option `options.includeCompiledRoute` is an optional boolean that defaults to true. When a caller passes `false` the handler skips `enrichCompiledRoutes()` on both the fresh and the cached return (`handlers/advisor-recommend.ts:563-565`, `632-634`), so no `compiled-route.cjs` subprocess starts and no recommendation carries `compiledRoute` or `command`. The prompt hooks pass `true` (`hooks/lib/skill-advisor-cli-fallback.ts:238`), because the `command` field is derived from the compiled route. The OpenCode plugin does not pass the option and keeps receiving `compiledRoute`. The option is declared in the zod schema (`schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts:287`), the tool descriptor (`tools/advisor-recommend.ts:23`) and the CLI manifest (`skill-advisor-cli-manifest.ts:57`).\n37:The request option `options.compiledRouteTopOnly` is an optional boolean that defaults to false. When a caller passes `true`, `enrichCompiledRoutes()` runs the route lookup for the first recommendation only and returns every later one unchanged, so only the top pick can carry `compiledRoute` or `command`. Each lookup is a `compiled-route.cjs` subprocess, so this saves one subprocess for each further eligible hub. The prompt hooks pass `true` with `includeCompiledRoute: true`, because the brief leads with the top pick. The option is declared in the zod schema (`schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts:290`), the tool descriptor (`tools/advisor-recommend.ts:24`) and the CLI manifest (`skill-advisor-cli-manifest.ts:58`).\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"295:    includeCompiledRoute: z.boolean().optional(),\n298:    compiledRouteTopOnly: z.boolean().optional(),\n321:  command: z.string().min(1).optional(),\n=== command field in recommendation schema ===\n321:  command: z.string().min(1).optional(),\n=== handler skips ===\n630:      input.options?.includeCompiledRoute === false\n705:    input.options?.includeCompiledRoute === false\n=== doc claims ===\n33:When a recommendation gets a `compiledRoute`, `enrichCompiledRoutes()` also asks `attachCommand()` in `lib/command-attach.ts` for a slash command and sets the optional `command` field when one comes back (`schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts:310`, `z.string().min(1).optional()`). `attachCommand()` names a command only for a `route` decision with `selectionKind: 'single'` and exactly one target, and only when the generated `MODE_COMMANDS` table maps that hub and `workflowMode` to a command. A bundle, a multi-target route or a mode with no command leaves `command` off. For `system-deep-loop` the prompt must type the same command or hold a phrase from `DEPTH_WORDING`, so a prompt that only names a topic such as research or review gets no deep-loop command. A prompt that matches `NO_EDIT_REQUEST` gets no command from any hub, because a reader who rules out a change is never handed work that writes.\n35:The request option `options.includeCompiledRoute` is an optional boolean that defaults to true. When a caller passes `false` the handler skips `enrichCompiledRoutes()` on both the fresh and the cached return (`handlers/advisor-recommend.ts:563-565`, `632-634`), so no `compiled-route.cjs` subprocess starts and no recommendation carries `compiledRoute` or `command`. The prompt hooks pass `true` (`hooks/lib/skill-advisor-cli-fallback.ts:238`), because the `command` field is derived from the compiled route. The OpenCode plugin does not pass the option and keeps receiving `compiledRoute`. The option is declared in the zod schema (`schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts:287`), the tool descriptor (`tools/advisor-recommend.ts:23`) and the CLI manifest (`skill-advisor-cli-manifest.ts:57`).\n37:The request option `options.compiledRouteTopOnly` is an optional boolean that defaults to false. When a caller passes `true`, `enrichCompiledRoutes()` runs the route lookup for the first recommendation only and returns every later one unchanged, so only the top pick can carry `compiledRoute` or `command`. Each lookup is a `compiled-route.cjs` subprocess, so this saves one subprocess for each further eligible hub. The prompt hooks pass `true` with `includeCompiledRoute: true`, because the brief leads with the top pick. The option is declared in the zod schema (`schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts:290`), the tool descriptor (`tools/advisor-recommend.ts:24`) and the CLI manifest (`skill-advisor-cli-manifest.ts:58`).\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && grep -n \\\"includeCompiledRoute: z.boolean\\\\|compiledRouteTopOnly: z.boolean\\\\|command: z.string().min(1).optional()\\\\|const options = patternString\\\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts | head; echo \\\"=== command field in recommendation schema ===\\\"; grep -n \\\"command:\\\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts | head; echo \\\"=== handler skips ===\\\"; grep -n \\\"includeCompiledRoute === false\\\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/handlers/advisor-recommend.ts; echo \\\"=== doc claims ===\\\"; grep -n \\\"advisor-tool-schemas.ts:287\\\\|advisor-tool-schemas.ts:290\\\\|advisor-tool-schemas.ts:310\\\\|advisor-recommend.ts:563-565\\\\|advisor-recommend.ts:632-634\\\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/cli-surface/advisor-recommend.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794571316249,"end":1794571318739}}}}
