{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794571381962,"sessionID":"ses_e2b4a243affexa25EPiSDt2Sxc","part":{"partID":"prt_1d4c9b661002TBiJ9D2ObZ1U6j","sessionID":"ses_e2b4a243affexa25EPiSDt2Sxc","messageID":"msg_1d4c990ed0018uAhbX6Ii7w7fQ","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-a06718dcb47bc846","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Review Iteration 004\n\n## Dispatcher\n\n- Mode: review (fan-out lineage `render-hooks-plugin-2`, pass two)\n- Session: `fanout-render-hooks-plugin-2-1794570021136-noekp0`, generation 1, lineage mode `new`\n- Review target: `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build`\n- Area: `render-hooks-plugin` — the `yes` documentation in this area plus the shared docs that describe the command brief\n- Operator review focus addressed this iteration: \"docs that disagree with code\", and pass-one fix verification for the documentation findings in this area (`R3-P2-002--ecbea1260371`, `Q2`) and the shared doc fixes (`R3-P2-001--0e0d904eb571`, `R3-P2-002--5522ea1fe8dd`).\n- Budget profile: `verify` (10 analysis actions)\n\n## Files Reviewed\n\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/cli-surface/advisor-recommend.md:26-70` — compiled-route enrichment, the two request options, the recommendation contract, the file table\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/hooks-and-plugin/claude-hook.md:20-45` — CLI request options and diagnostics paragraph\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md:30-125`, `:170-195` — brief head form, degraded contract, runtime table, OpenCode tuning, diagnostics row\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/ARCHITECTURE.md:139-146` — hook and plugin integration paragraph\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/README.md:174-176` — command-row count\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/command-meaning-matching.md:24-28` — command-row count\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts:285-322` — the cited schema fields\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/handlers/advisor-recommend.ts:626-636`, `:700-710` — the cited skip ranges\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/skill-advisor-cli.ts:1529-1556` — the `-32602` retry that the hook reference describes\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:190-245` — `commandRowFor` own-key lookup and the `TRACKED_COMMANDS` policy source\n\n## Findings - New\n\n### P0 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n### P1 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n### P2 Findings\n\n1. **Five line citations in `advisor-recommend.md` point at unrelated code** -- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/cli-surface/advisor-recommend.md:33` -- The rewritten enrichment section cites `schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts:310` for the `command` field, `:287` for `includeCompiledRoute` and `:290` for `compiledRouteTopOnly`, and `handlers/advisor-recommend.ts:563-565` / `:632-634` for the two skip branches. The first three land on `skillId` (`:321` is the field), `workspaceRoot` (`:295` is the field) and `topK` (`:298` is the field); the handler ranges land on `outputAbstainReasons` and the `enrichCompiledRoutes` call (`:630-632` and `:705-707` are the two skips).\nCase: a reader opens §\"Compiled-Routing Enrichment\" and follows `schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts:287` to learn what `includeCompiledRoute` validates; the line is `workspaceRoot: BoundedWorkspaceRootSchema.optional()`, and the same call at `:310` is `skillId: z.string().min(1)`. The other three citations are off in the same way.\nFinding class: documentation traceability\nScope proof: `grep -n` over the two cited files returns the actual field and skip lines; every cited line was read directly and the mismatched token at each is named above.\nAffected surface hints: `advisor-recommend.md` sections \"Compiled-Routing Enrichment\" and the two option paragraphs; the same schema offsets are likely cited by the CLI-surface leaf in other areas.\n\n## Withdrawn Finding\n\n**`iter2-P2-hook-health-doc-scope` is withdrawn.** Iteration 2 read `skill-advisor-hook-validation.md:100` (\"Every hook run writes a prompt-free health record\") as covering the OpenCode plugin. It does not: the sentence is scoped to hook runs, and every hook adapter reaches the same handler that persists the record — the Claude handler directly, Pi and DSH through `handleClaudeUserPromptSubmit` with a runtime label, and the Codex, Cursor and Devin shims through `runClaudeHookAdapter`, which sets `SPECKIT_RUNTIME` before spawning the compiled handler (`system-spec-kit/runtime/hooks/devin/shared.ts:95-110`). The OpenCode plugin is a plugin, not a hook, and the playbook covers it in its own Step 4. The finding over-read the sentence; recorded as resolved in this iteration's state record so the merged report does not carry it.\n\n## Pass-One Fix Verification\n\n- **Q2 (`advisor-recommend.md:45`, name `TRACKED_COMMANDS[command].policy`) — fix holds.** The Recommendation Contract paragraph at `:51` now says \"A command attached through the compiled route takes its `policy` from `TRACKED_COMMANDS[command].policy`, the table keyed by runnable string that covers every tracked command\". `command-attach.ts:242` is that lookup.\n- **R3-P2-002--ecbea1260371 (`advisor-recommend.md:45`, document `mutating`) — fix holds.** The same paragraph documents `{ command, policy?, mutating?, ownerSkillId }` and names `mutating` as the class the renderer's child downgrade reads, with `/doctor:env list` as the read-only example. The renderer's `parentNamedOnly` matches that rule.\n- **R3-P2-001--0e0d904eb571 (README and `command-meaning-matching.md` say 46 rows) — fix holds.** `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/README.md:176` says \"46 command rows\" and `feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/command-meaning-matching.md:26` says \"46 rows in all\". No other count appears in either paragraph.\n- **R3-P2-002--5522ea1fe8dd (ARCHITECTURE names the DSH adapter) — fix holds.** `ARCHITECTURE.md:143` names `hooks/dsh/prompt-advisor.mjs` and states it runs the Claude handler from `runtime/dist/hooks/claude/user-prompt-submit.js`.\n- **The hook reference's `-32602` retry claim holds.** `skill-advisor-cli.ts:1529-1556` drops both compiled-route keys when the rejected list names `includeCompiledRoute`, and otherwise drops the keys the daemon named; the doc says \"retries once without them\".\n\n## Traceability Checks\n\n| Protocol | Level | Status | Notes |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `spec_code` | core | pass | The three new documentation sections (`Recommendation Contract`, brief head form, degraded contract) match the code read in iterations 1-3. |\n| `checklist_evidence` | core | notApplicable | No checklist row governs the documentation pass. |\n| `skill_agent` | overlay | notApplicable | No agent definition in this area. |\n| `agent_cross_runtime` | overlay | pass | `skill-advisor-hook.md` adds the DSH row and a per-runtime command-start table; the runtime rows match `ARCHITECTURE.md:143` and the adapter files. |\n| `feature_catalog_code` | overlay | partial | The catalog leaf matches the code in substance; finding 1 is its line-citation drift. |\n| `playbook_capability` | overlay | pass | The validation playbook's changed diagnostics sentence survives the withdrawal above: every hook adapter persists. |\n\n## Integration Evidence\n\n- CLI option contract: `runtime/schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts:295`, `:298`, `:321`; retry at `runtime/skill-advisor-cli.ts:1529-1556`; hook payload at `hooks/lib/skill-advisor-cli-fallback.ts:238-241`.\n- Renderer contract: `runtime/lib/render.ts:219-246` (label), `:557-560` (`needs a mode`), `:529` (`AI_SESSION_CHILD`).\n- Runtime adapters named by the doc: `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/dsh/prompt-advisor.mjs`, `hooks/pi/prompt-advisor.ts`, `.opencode/plugins/system-skill-advisor.js`, and the system-spec-kit shims at `.skilled/hooks/skill-advisor/{claude,codex,cursor,devin}/`.\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n- **`SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_COMPILED_ROUTE_BOUNDING` is documented as status-only.** `skill-advisor-hook.md:176` says the variable is \"kept for existing configs: the transform adds no compiled-route line, so it changes only the `bounded_compiled_route_summary` status field\". That confirms the behavior iteration 2 recorded and narrows it: the defect is the plugin's own jsdoc (`system-skill-advisor.js:1080`) still saying \"Bound long compiled-route target lists\", not the env var's existence. Finding `iter2-P2-inert-bounded-summary-option` stands on the jsdoc wording and the status field.\n- **`claude-hook.md` lists the status vocabulary without `stale`.** `metrics.ts:24` includes `stale` in `ADVISOR_HOOK_STATUS_VALUES`. The sentence predates this pass and is unchanged by it; not reported here to keep pass two to defects the change introduced or re-exposed.\n- **The command-start table in `skill-advisor-hook.md:104-115` is not code-verifiable in this pass.** It describes model-side tool reach per runtime (for example 33 of 45 names for Claude Code); no repository artifact can confirm the host's tool list, and the pass already covers the runtime routing itself. Recorded as unverified, not as a finding.\n\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\n\n- The brief head form documented at `skill-advisor-hook.md:74-90` matches `commandLabel` and `policyWord` exactly: `owner → command (policy)`, no parenthesis when the policy is unknown, `(needs a mode)` when the hub withheld its command.\n- The degraded contract documented at `:92-100` matches `recommendationFromCli` and the degraded path: a typed bare slash command keeps the command fields, every other row collapses to its owner skill.\n- `advisor-recommend.md:33` accurately describes `attachCommand`'s gates (`route`, `selectionKind: 'single'`, one target, `MODE_COMMANDS`, `DEPTH_WORDING`, `NO_EDIT_REQUEST`).\n- The shared doc rows for the runtime adapters match `ARCHITECTURE.md` and the adapter files.\n\n## Ruled Out\n\n- **The OpenCode plugin's missing health record is a doc defect.** Withdrawn above: the changed sentence is about hook runs, and the plugin is a separate delivery path with its own playbook step.\n- **The documented `includeCompiledRoute` default contradicts the hook's explicit `true`.** Not a contradiction: the option defaults to true and the hook states its explicit value and why, in both `claude-hook.md:26` and `skill-advisor-hook.md:38`.\n- **The catalog's `command` field claim overstates the schema.** `command: z.string().min(1).optional()` exists at `advisor-tool-schemas.ts:321`; only its citation is wrong.\n\n## Next Focus\n\n- Dimension: maintainability\n- Focus area: the remaining `yes` code in this area — `.opencode/plugins/system-skill-advisor.js` mapper and transform, `hooks/lib/skill-advisor-cli-fallback.ts` structure, `runtime/lib/metrics.ts`, and the runtime-mirror sync scripts with their tests.\n- Reason: correctness, security and traceability are covered; maintainability is the last dimension, and the plugin/fallback changes left dead or duplicate surfaces worth one pass.\n- Rotation status: dimension 4 of 4.\n- Blocked/productive carry-forward: none.\n- Required evidence: the diffs already read plus one direct read of each remaining changed block; no new scan of the whole tree.\n\nReview verdict: PASS\n","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/render-hooks-plugin-2/iterations/iteration-004.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/render-hooks-plugin-2/iterations/iteration-004.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/render-hooks-plugin-2/iterations/iteration-004.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\": \"# Review Iteration 004\\n\\n## Dispatcher\\n\\n- Mode: review (fan-out lineage `render-hooks-plugin-2`, pass two)\\n- Session: `fanout-render-hooks-plugin-2-1794570021136-noekp0`, generation 1, lineage mode `new`\\n- Review target: `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build`\\n- Area: `render-hooks-plugin` — the `yes` documentation in this area plus the shared docs that describe the command brief\\n- Operator review focus addressed this iteration: \\\"docs that disagree with code\\\", and pass-one fix verification for the documentation findings in this area (`R3-P2-002--ecbea1260371`, `Q2`) and the shared doc fixes (`R3-P2-001--0e0d904eb571`, `R3-P2-002--5522ea1fe8dd`).\\n- Budget profile: `verify` (10 analysis actions)\\n\\n## Files Reviewed\\n\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/cli-surface/advisor-recommend.md:26-70` — compiled-route enrichment, the two request options, the recommendation contract, the file table\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/hooks-and-plugin/claude-hook.md:20-45` — CLI request options and diagnostics paragraph\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md:30-125`, `:170-195` — brief head form, degraded contract, runtime table, OpenCode tuning, diagnostics row\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/ARCHITECTURE.md:139-146` — hook and plugin integration paragraph\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/README.md:174-176` — command-row count\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/command-meaning-matching.md:24-28` — command-row count\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts:285-322` — the cited schema fields\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/handlers/advisor-recommend.ts:626-636`, `:700-710` — the cited skip ranges\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/skill-advisor-cli.ts:1529-1556` — the `-32602` retry that the hook reference describes\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:190-245` — `commandRowFor` own-key lookup and the `TRACKED_COMMANDS` policy source\\n\\n## Findings - New\\n\\n### P0 Findings\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n### P1 Findings\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n### P2 Findings\\n\\n1. **Five line citations in `advisor-recommend.md` point at unrelated code** -- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/cli-surface/advisor-recommend.md:33` -- The rewritten enrichment section cites `schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts:310` for the `command` field, `:287` for `includeCompiledRoute` and `:290` for `compiledRouteTopOnly`, and `handlers/advisor-recommend.ts:563-565` / `:632-634` for the two skip branches. The first three land on `skillId` (`:321` is the field), `workspaceRoot` (`:295` is the field) and `topK` (`:298` is the field); the handler ranges land on `outputAbstainReasons` and the `enrichCompiledRoutes` call (`:630-632` and `:705-707` are the two skips).\\nCase: a reader opens §\\\"Compiled-Routing Enrichment\\\" and follows `schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts:287` to learn what `includeCompiledRoute` validates; the line is `workspaceRoot: BoundedWorkspaceRootSchema.optional()`, and the same call at `:310` is `skillId: z.string().min(1)`. The other three citations are off in the same way.\\nFinding class: documentation traceability\\nScope proof: `grep -n` over the two cited files returns the actual field and skip lines; every cited line was read directly and the mismatched token at each is named above.\\nAffected surface hints: `advisor-recommend.md` sections \\\"Compiled-Routing Enrichment\\\" and the two option paragraphs; the same schema offsets are likely cited by the CLI-surface leaf in other areas.\\n\\n## Withdrawn Finding\\n\\n**`iter2-P2-hook-health-doc-scope` is withdrawn.** Iteration 2 read `skill-advisor-hook-validation.md:100` (\\\"Every hook run writes a prompt-free health record\\\") as covering the OpenCode plugin. It does not: the sentence is scoped to hook runs, and every hook adapter reaches the same handler that persists the record — the Claude handler directly, Pi and DSH through `handleClaudeUserPromptSubmit` with a runtime label, and the Codex, Cursor and Devin shims through `runClaudeHookAdapter`, which sets `SPECKIT_RUNTIME` before spawning the compiled handler (`system-spec-kit/runtime/hooks/devin/shared.ts:95-110`). The OpenCode plugin is a plugin, not a hook, and the playbook covers it in its own Step 4. The finding over-read the sentence; recorded as resolved in this iteration's state record so the merged report does not carry it.\\n\\n## Pass-One Fix Verification\\n\\n- **Q2 (`advisor-recommend.md:45`, name `TRACKED_COMMANDS[command].policy`) — fix holds.** The Recommendation Contract paragraph at `:51` now says \\\"A command attached through the compiled route takes its `policy` from `TRACKED_COMMANDS[command].policy`, the table keyed by runnable string that covers every tracked command\\\". `command-attach.ts:242` is that lookup.\\n- **R3-P2-002--ecbea1260371 (`advisor-recommend.md:45`, document `mutating`) — fix holds.** The same paragraph documents `{ command, policy?, mutating?, ownerSkillId }` and names `mutating` as the class the renderer's child downgrade reads, with `/doctor:env list` as the read-only example. The renderer's `parentNamedOnly` matches that rule.\\n- **R3-P2-001--0e0d904eb571 (README and `command-meaning-matching.md` say 46 rows) — fix holds.** `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/README.md:176` says \\\"46 command rows\\\" and `feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/command-meaning-matching.md:26` says \\\"46 rows in all\\\". No other count appears in either paragraph.\\n- **R3-P2-002--5522ea1fe8dd (ARCHITECTURE names the DSH adapter) — fix holds.** `ARCHITECTURE.md:143` names `hooks/dsh/prompt-advisor.mjs` and states it runs the Claude handler from `runtime/dist/hooks/claude/user-prompt-submit.js`.\\n- **The hook reference's `-32602` retry claim holds.** `skill-advisor-cli.ts:1529-1556` drops both compiled-route keys when the rejected list names `includeCompiledRoute`, and otherwise drops the keys the daemon named; the doc says \\\"retries once without them\\\".\\n\\n## Traceability Checks\\n\\n| Protocol | Level | Status | Notes |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| `spec_code` | core | pass | The three new documentation sections (`Recommendation Contract`, brief head form, degraded contract) match the code read in iterations 1-3. |\\n| `checklist_evidence` | core | notApplicable | No checklist row governs the documentation pass. |\\n| `skill_agent` | overlay | notApplicable | No agent definition in this area. |\\n| `agent_cross_runtime` | overlay | pass | `skill-advisor-hook.md` adds the DSH row and a per-runtime command-start table; the runtime rows match `ARCHITECTURE.md:143` and the adapter files. |\\n| `feature_catalog_code` | overlay | partial | The catalog leaf matches the code in substance; finding 1 is its line-citation drift. |\\n| `playbook_capability` | overlay | pass | The validation playbook's changed diagnostics sentence survives the withdrawal above: every hook adapter persists. |\\n\\n## Integration Evidence\\n\\n- CLI option contract: `runtime/schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts:295`, `:298`, `:321`; retry at `runtime/skill-advisor-cli.ts:1529-1556`; hook payload at `hooks/lib/skill-advisor-cli-fallback.ts:238-241`.\\n- Renderer contract: `runtime/lib/render.ts:219-246` (label), `:557-560` (`needs a mode`), `:529` (`AI_SESSION_CHILD`).\\n- Runtime adapters named by the doc: `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/dsh/prompt-advisor.mjs`, `hooks/pi/prompt-advisor.ts`, `.opencode/plugins/system-skill-advisor.js`, and the system-spec-kit shims at `.skilled/hooks/skill-advisor/{claude,codex,cursor,devin}/`.\\n\\n## Edge Cases\\n\\n- **`SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_COMPILED_ROUTE_BOUNDING` is documented as status-only.** `skill-advisor-hook.md:176` says the variable is \\\"kept for existing configs: the transform adds no compiled-route line, so it changes only the `bounded_compiled_route_summary` status field\\\". That confirms the behavior iteration 2 recorded and narrows it: the defect is the plugin's own jsdoc (`system-skill-advisor.js:1080`) still saying \\\"Bound long compiled-route target lists\\\", not the env var's existence. Finding `iter2-P2-inert-bounded-summary-option` stands on the jsdoc wording and the status field.\\n- **`claude-hook.md` lists the status vocabulary without `stale`.** `metrics.ts:24` includes `stale` in `ADVISOR_HOOK_STATUS_VALUES`. The sentence predates this pass and is unchanged by it; not reported here to keep pass two to defects the change introduced or re-exposed.\\n- **The command-start table in `skill-advisor-hook.md:104-115` is not code-verifiable in this pass.** It describes model-side tool reach per runtime (for example 33 of 45 names for Claude Code); no repository artifact can confirm the host's tool list, and the pass already covers the runtime routing itself. Recorded as unverified, not as a finding.\\n\\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\\n\\n- The brief head form documented at `skill-advisor-hook.md:74-90` matches `commandLabel` and `policyWord` exactly: `owner → command (policy)`, no parenthesis when the policy is unknown, `(needs a mode)` when the hub withheld its command.\\n- The degraded contract documented at `:92-100` matches `recommendationFromCli` and the degraded path: a typed bare slash command keeps the command fields, every other row collapses to its owner skill.\\n- `advisor-recommend.md:33` accurately describes `attachCommand`'s gates (`route`, `selectionKind: 'single'`, one target, `MODE_COMMANDS`, `DEPTH_WORDING`, `NO_EDIT_REQUEST`).\\n- The shared doc rows for the runtime adapters match `ARCHITECTURE.md` and the adapter files.\\n\\n## Ruled Out\\n\\n- **The OpenCode plugin's missing health record is a doc defect.** Withdrawn above: the changed sentence is about hook runs, and the plugin is a separate delivery path with its own playbook step.\\n- **The documented `includeCompiledRoute` default contradicts the hook's explicit `true`.** Not a contradiction: the option defaults to true and the hook states its explicit value and why, in both `claude-hook.md:26` and `skill-advisor-hook.md:38`.\\n- **The catalog's `command` field claim overstates the schema.** `command: z.string().min(1).optional()` exists at `advisor-tool-schemas.ts:321`; only its citation is wrong.\\n\\n## Next Focus\\n\\n- Dimension: maintainability\\n- Focus area: the remaining `yes` code in this area — `.opencode/plugins/system-skill-advisor.js` mapper and transform, `hooks/lib/skill-advisor-cli-fallback.ts` structure, `runtime/lib/metrics.ts`, and the runtime-mirror sync scripts with their tests.\\n- Reason: correctness, security and traceability are covered; maintainability is the last dimension, and the plugin/fallback changes left dead or duplicate surfaces worth one pass.\\n- Rotation status: dimension 4 of 4.\\n- Blocked/productive carry-forward: none.\\n- Required evidence: the diffs already read plus one direct read of each remaining changed block; no new scan of the whole tree.\\n\\nReview verdict: PASS\\n\", \"path\": \"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/render-hooks-plugin-2/iterations/iteration-004.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794571351649,"end":1794571381962}}}}
