{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794571443290,"sessionID":"ses_e2b4a243affexa25EPiSDt2Sxc","part":{"partID":"prt_1d4cb18c7001X5alQFCZu4jbuQ","sessionID":"ses_e2b4a243affexa25EPiSDt2Sxc","messageID":"msg_1d4cac9fb001z9zBOwoktuhJmt","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-a45f87a779703b86","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && git diff 35c3188681..HEAD -- .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/lib/README.md; echo \"=== current fallback README text ===\"; grep -n \"includeCompiledRoute\\|compiled\\|route\\|diagnostic\\|degraded\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/lib/README.md | head -20; echo \"=== MAX_STDOUT_BYTES ===\"; grep -n \"MAX_STDOUT_BYTES\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/lib/skill-advisor-cli-fallback.ts | head -3"},"output":"diff --git a/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/lib/README.md b/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/lib/README.md\nindex 6c76c35c0b..1ef0fd76c1 100644\n--- a/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/lib/README.md\n+++ b/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/lib/README.md\n@@ -1,7 +1,7 @@\n ---\n title: \"Hooks Lib: Skill Advisor CLI Fallback\"\n description: \"Warm-daemon CLI fallback that the skill-advisor prompt hook falls back to when the in-process advisor brief comes back empty.\"\n-version: 1.0.0.0\n+version: 1.0.1.0\n ---\n \n # Hooks Lib: Skill Advisor CLI Fallback\n@@ -18,7 +18,7 @@ version: 1.0.0.0\n \n | File | Purpose |\n |------|---------|\n-| `skill-advisor-cli-fallback.ts` | Resolves the CLI, IPC bridge and database paths from one root (`.skilled`, then `.opencode`), spawns the advisor CLI with a bounded timeout. It sends the request on stdin with `--json -`, so the prompt never appears in the child's argv. The request it sends carries `options.includeCompiledRoute: false`, so the daemon skips compiled-route enrichment and starts no `compiled-route.cjs` child. It runs the CLI with `--no-warm-only`, because the CLI is the component that starts the daemon on a cold socket. It parses its JSON payload and normalizes the result (and retryable exit/reason codes) into an `AdvisorHookResult`. |\n+| `skill-advisor-cli-fallback.ts` | Resolves the CLI, IPC bridge and database paths from one root (`.skilled`, then `.opencode`), spawns the advisor CLI with a bounded timeout. It sends the request on stdin with `--json -`, so the prompt never appears in the child's argv. The request it sends carries `options.includeCompiledRoute: true`, because the advisor derives a recommendation's slash command from the compiled route, and `options.compiledRouteTopOnly: true`, so only the top pick gets a route lookup. `recommendationFromCli` keeps a non-empty `command` on each recommendation and reads nothing from the route itself. It runs the CLI with `--no-warm-only`, because the CLI is the component that starts the daemon on a cold socket. It parses its JSON payload and normalizes the result (and retryable exit/reason codes) into an `AdvisorHookResult`. |\n \n ---\n \n=== current fallback README text ===\n13:`hooks/lib/` holds the CLI fallback path for the `system-skill-advisor` prompt hook. When the in-process advisor brief returns `fail_open` or a degraded, unavailable-freshness result, this module finds the advisor CLI under `.skilled` first and `.opencode` second, takes the CLI, its IPC bridge and the database directory from that one root, shells out to `<root>/bin/skill-advisor.cjs advisor_recommend` and reshapes the CLI response back into the same `AdvisorHookResult` envelope the hook already understands. The CLI starts the daemon itself when the socket is cold, so a cold in-process path does not have to mean a silent miss.\n21:| `skill-advisor-cli-fallback.ts` | Resolves the CLI, IPC bridge and database paths from one root (`.skilled`, then `.opencode`), spawns the advisor CLI with a bounded timeout. It sends the request on stdin with `--json -`, so the prompt never appears in the child's argv. The request it sends carries `options.includeCompiledRoute: true`, because the advisor derives a recommendation's slash command from the compiled route, and `options.compiledRouteTopOnly: true`, so only the top pick gets a route lookup. `recommendationFromCli` keeps a non-empty `command` on each recommendation and reads nothing from the route itself. It runs the CLI with `--no-warm-only`, because the CLI is the component that starts the daemon on a cold socket. It parses its JSON payload and normalizes the result (and retryable exit/reason codes) into an `AdvisorHookResult`. |\n=== MAX_STDOUT_BYTES ===\n92:const MAX_STDOUT_BYTES = 1024 * 1024;\n215:  if (current.length >= MAX_STDOUT_BYTES) {\n218:  return (current + chunk).slice(0, MAX_STDOUT_BYTES);\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"diff --git a/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/lib/README.md b/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/lib/README.md\nindex 6c76c35c0b..1ef0fd76c1 100644\n--- a/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/lib/README.md\n+++ b/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/lib/README.md\n@@ -1,7 +1,7 @@\n ---\n title: \"Hooks Lib: Skill Advisor CLI Fallback\"\n description: \"Warm-daemon CLI fallback that the skill-advisor prompt hook falls back to when the in-process advisor brief comes back empty.\"\n-version: 1.0.0.0\n+version: 1.0.1.0\n ---\n \n # Hooks Lib: Skill Advisor CLI Fallback\n@@ -18,7 +18,7 @@ version: 1.0.0.0\n \n | File | Purpose |\n |------|---------|\n-| `skill-advisor-cli-fallback.ts` | Resolves the CLI, IPC bridge and database paths from one root (`.skilled`, then `.opencode`), spawns the advisor CLI with a bounded timeout. It sends the request on stdin with `--json -`, so the prompt never appears in the child's argv. The request it sends carries `options.includeCompiledRoute: false`, so the daemon skips compiled-route enrichment and starts no `compiled-route.cjs` child. It runs the CLI with `--no-warm-only`, because the CLI is the component that starts the daemon on a cold socket. It parses its JSON payload and normalizes the result (and retryable exit/reason codes) into an `AdvisorHookResult`. |\n+| `skill-advisor-cli-fallback.ts` | Resolves the CLI, IPC bridge and database paths from one root (`.skilled`, then `.opencode`), spawns the advisor CLI with a bounded timeout. It sends the request on stdin with `--json -`, so the prompt never appears in the child's argv. The request it sends carries `options.includeCompiledRoute: true`, because the advisor derives a recommendation's slash command from the compiled route, and `options.compiledRouteTopOnly: true`, so only the top pick gets a route lookup. `recommendationFromCli` keeps a non-empty `command` on each recommendation and reads nothing from the route itself. It runs the CLI with `--no-warm-only`, because the CLI is the component that starts the daemon on a cold socket. It parses its JSON payload and normalizes the result (and retryable exit/reason codes) into an `AdvisorHookResult`. |\n \n ---\n \n=== current fallback README text ===\n13:`hooks/lib/` holds the CLI fallback path for the `system-skill-advisor` prompt hook. When the in-process advisor brief returns `fail_open` or a degraded, unavailable-freshness result, this module finds the advisor CLI under `.skilled` first and `.opencode` second, takes the CLI, its IPC bridge and the database directory from that one root, shells out to `<root>/bin/skill-advisor.cjs advisor_recommend` and reshapes the CLI response back into the same `AdvisorHookResult` envelope the hook already understands. The CLI starts the daemon itself when the socket is cold, so a cold in-process path does not have to mean a silent miss.\n21:| `skill-advisor-cli-fallback.ts` | Resolves the CLI, IPC bridge and database paths from one root (`.skilled`, then `.opencode`), spawns the advisor CLI with a bounded timeout. It sends the request on stdin with `--json -`, so the prompt never appears in the child's argv. The request it sends carries `options.includeCompiledRoute: true`, because the advisor derives a recommendation's slash command from the compiled route, and `options.compiledRouteTopOnly: true`, so only the top pick gets a route lookup. `recommendationFromCli` keeps a non-empty `command` on each recommendation and reads nothing from the route itself. It runs the CLI with `--no-warm-only`, because the CLI is the component that starts the daemon on a cold socket. It parses its JSON payload and normalizes the result (and retryable exit/reason codes) into an `AdvisorHookResult`. |\n=== MAX_STDOUT_BYTES ===\n92:const MAX_STDOUT_BYTES = 1024 * 1024;\n215:  if (current.length >= MAX_STDOUT_BYTES) {\n218:  return (current + chunk).slice(0, MAX_STDOUT_BYTES);\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && git diff 35c3188681..HEAD -- .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/lib/README.md; echo \\\"=== current fallback README text ===\\\"; grep -n \\\"includeCompiledRoute\\\\|compiled\\\\|route\\\\|diagnostic\\\\|degraded\\\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/lib/README.md | head -20; echo \\\"=== MAX_STDOUT_BYTES ===\\\"; grep -n \\\"MAX_STDOUT_BYTES\\\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/lib/skill-advisor-cli-fallback.ts | head -3\"}"},"time":{"start":1794571442375,"end":1794571443290}}}}
