{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794571701427,"sessionID":"ses_e2b4a243affexa25EPiSDt2Sxc","part":{"id":"prt_1d4cf0cb30011Gvn6vrtElEKd1","sessionID":"ses_e2b4a243affexa25EPiSDt2Sxc","messageID":"msg_1d4cef65f001iebb8rLxWoBpP7","type":"step-start","snapshot":"95186603ecd6d614ecdb221dfd96289684ecb6c4"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794571720935,"sessionID":"ses_e2b4a243affexa25EPiSDt2Sxc","part":{"partID":"prt_1d4cf0cc7002mtO2BaCGH4SkbU","sessionID":"ses_e2b4a243affexa25EPiSDt2Sxc","messageID":"msg_1d4cef65f001iebb8rLxWoBpP7","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-9ce33ba6b145c898","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Review Iteration 006\n\n## Dispatcher\n\n- Mode: review (fan-out lineage `render-hooks-plugin-2`, pass two)\n- Session: `fanout-render-hooks-plugin-2-1794570021136-noekp0`, generation 1, lineage mode `new`\n- Review target: `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build`\n- Area: `render-hooks-plugin` — cross-reference sweep over every open finding and the remaining changed exits\n- Operator review focus addressed this iteration: the sweep re-reads every open finding's anchor line, proves the hook diagnostics claim at its exit points, and states the holdout counts without reading holdout text.\n- Budget profile: `adjudicate` (9 analysis actions)\n\n## Files Reviewed\n\n- `.opencode/plugins/system-skill-advisor.js:657`, `:669`, `:1704` — orphaned summary and the status field\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/subprocess.ts:144-150`, `:250-255` — stderr cap and both handlers\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook-validation.md:100` — the changed health-record sentence (withdrawn finding)\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/claude/user-prompt-submit.ts:296-465` — every exit that emits a diagnostic record\n- `runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-prompts.jsonl` and `holdout-prompts.jsonl` — line counts only\n- Test files already read in iterations 1-5; no new read needed for the sweep\n\n## Findings - New\n\n### P0 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n### P1 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n### P2 Findings\n\nNone. The five open P2 findings stand as recorded; no new defect and no severity movement.\n\n## Open Finding Re-Check\n\n- **`iter2-P2-inert-bounded-summary-option`** (`.opencode/plugins/system-skill-advisor.js:379`) — re-read: `boundedCompiledRouteSummary` is resolved at `:379-395` from the option or `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_COMPILED_ROUTE_BOUNDING`, documented at `:1080` as \"Bound long compiled-route target lists\", and reported at `:1704`; the transform block that consumed it is gone (`:1582-1590`). No reader remains. P2 stands.\n- **`iter2-P2-stderr-cap-hides-busy`** (`.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/subprocess.ts:144`) — re-read: `capOutput` drops bytes after `MAX_OUTPUT_CHARS` on both streams, and the busy marker is read from the accumulated `stderr`. The new test asserts the lost marker. P2 stands.\n- **`iter4-P2-advisor-recommend-stale-line-refs`** (`.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/cli-surface/advisor-recommend.md:33`) — re-read: the five citations stay wrong against `advisor-tool-schemas.ts:295/298/321` and `handlers/advisor-recommend.ts:630-632/705-707`. P2 stands.\n- **`iter5-P2-orphaned-route-summary`** (`.opencode/plugins/system-skill-advisor.js:657`) — re-read: `compiledRouteSummary(data)` still runs per delivered brief and the `metadata.compiledRouteSummary` field at `:669` has no reader in `.opencode`. P2 stands.\n- **`iter5-P2-field-pass-through-untested`** (`.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/hooks/skill-advisor-cli-fallback-envelope.vitest.ts:49`) — re-read: the test's command-bearing case sends no `command`/`policy`/`ownerSkillId`, and the plugin tests assert none of the four fields. P2 stands.\n\nNo finding is a P0 or P1, so the verdict stays PASS with advisories.\n\n## Traceability Checks\n\n| Protocol | Level | Status | Notes |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `spec_code` | core | pass | Every doc claim that changed in this area was checked against its code line; only the citations in finding 3 are wrong. |\n| `checklist_evidence` | core | notApplicable | No checklist row governs this code pass. |\n| `skill_agent` | overlay | notApplicable | No agent definition in this area. |\n| `agent_cross_runtime` | overlay | pass | The six named runtimes resolve to the shared handler (claude/codex/cursor/devin/pi/dsh) or the plugin; both command-label paths carry the same fields. |\n| `feature_catalog_code` | overlay | partial | The catalog leaf matches in substance; finding 3 is its citation drift. |\n| `playbook_capability` | overlay | pass | The validation playbook's health-record sentence holds at every hook exit (see below). |\n\n## Integration Evidence\n\n- Hook exits that emit a health record: the kill-switch/prompt-gate branches (`user-prompt-submit.ts:302`, `:314`, `:330`), the delivered-brief branch (`:416`), the unhandled-exception branch (`:451`), and the fallback branch (`:514`). Each precedes its `return`, so every prompt path persists one record.\n- Holdout hygiene counts: `command-prompts.jsonl` holds 176 rows and `holdout-prompts.jsonl` holds 66. No file in this area opens either fixture; no row text was read or printed in this lineage.\n- The `.d.mts.map` artifacts are generated declaration maps; the four `yes` files were not read line by line, as recorded in iteration 5.\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n- **No new edge case.** The sweep found the same two removal residues and the same documentation offsets already recorded; nothing new was admitted.\n- **Synthesis cycle.** Convergence at this iteration (no new findings, all four dimensions covered) means the next phase is synthesis, not a seventh iteration.\n\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\n\n- The child-session downgrade is still the only reader of `AI_SESSION_CHILD` in the advisor (`render.ts:529`); tests stub it in both golden files and the fallback envelope test, and the parity case compares it with `isChildSession`.\n- The plugin's mapper and the hook fallback mapper agree on the four forwarded fields; the gap is test coverage, not behavior.\n- The subprocess cap is the only bounded-output change in this area and both streams pass through it.\n- The reader layer's containment is enforced before every read (iteration 3).\n\n## Ruled Out\n\n- **Any of the five open findings is a P0/P1.** Each is advisory: no data loss on a default path, no security boundary crossed, and each has a named concrete input. Verdict PASS.\n- **The hook's health record misses a prompt path.** All six emit sites precede their returns, so skipped, delivered, fallback and exception paths all persist.\n- **A seventh iteration would find something new.** The remaining unread artifacts are generated declaration maps and tests already read; the changed set is exhausted.\n\n## Next Focus\n\n- Dimension: synthesis\n- Focus area: compile the lineage report from the registry and the six iterations; no further code review.\n- Reason: convergence reached with all four dimensions covered and five active P2 advisories.\n- Rotation status: all four dimensions complete.\n- Blocked/productive carry-forward: none.\n- Required evidence: the reducer-owned registry, the six iteration files and their deltas.\n\nReview verdict: PASS\n","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/render-hooks-plugin-2/iterations/iteration-006.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/render-hooks-plugin-2/iterations/iteration-006.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/render-hooks-plugin-2/iterations/iteration-006.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\": \"# Review Iteration 006\\n\\n## Dispatcher\\n\\n- Mode: review (fan-out lineage `render-hooks-plugin-2`, pass two)\\n- Session: `fanout-render-hooks-plugin-2-1794570021136-noekp0`, generation 1, lineage mode `new`\\n- Review target: `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build`\\n- Area: `render-hooks-plugin` — cross-reference sweep over every open finding and the remaining changed exits\\n- Operator review focus addressed this iteration: the sweep re-reads every open finding's anchor line, proves the hook diagnostics claim at its exit points, and states the holdout counts without reading holdout text.\\n- Budget profile: `adjudicate` (9 analysis actions)\\n\\n## Files Reviewed\\n\\n- `.opencode/plugins/system-skill-advisor.js:657`, `:669`, `:1704` — orphaned summary and the status field\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/subprocess.ts:144-150`, `:250-255` — stderr cap and both handlers\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook-validation.md:100` — the changed health-record sentence (withdrawn finding)\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/claude/user-prompt-submit.ts:296-465` — every exit that emits a diagnostic record\\n- `runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-prompts.jsonl` and `holdout-prompts.jsonl` — line counts only\\n- Test files already read in iterations 1-5; no new read needed for the sweep\\n\\n## Findings - New\\n\\n### P0 Findings\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n### P1 Findings\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n### P2 Findings\\n\\nNone. The five open P2 findings stand as recorded; no new defect and no severity movement.\\n\\n## Open Finding Re-Check\\n\\n- **`iter2-P2-inert-bounded-summary-option`** (`.opencode/plugins/system-skill-advisor.js:379`) — re-read: `boundedCompiledRouteSummary` is resolved at `:379-395` from the option or `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_COMPILED_ROUTE_BOUNDING`, documented at `:1080` as \\\"Bound long compiled-route target lists\\\", and reported at `:1704`; the transform block that consumed it is gone (`:1582-1590`). No reader remains. P2 stands.\\n- **`iter2-P2-stderr-cap-hides-busy`** (`.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/subprocess.ts:144`) — re-read: `capOutput` drops bytes after `MAX_OUTPUT_CHARS` on both streams, and the busy marker is read from the accumulated `stderr`. The new test asserts the lost marker. P2 stands.\\n- **`iter4-P2-advisor-recommend-stale-line-refs`** (`.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/cli-surface/advisor-recommend.md:33`) — re-read: the five citations stay wrong against `advisor-tool-schemas.ts:295/298/321` and `handlers/advisor-recommend.ts:630-632/705-707`. P2 stands.\\n- **`iter5-P2-orphaned-route-summary`** (`.opencode/plugins/system-skill-advisor.js:657`) — re-read: `compiledRouteSummary(data)` still runs per delivered brief and the `metadata.compiledRouteSummary` field at `:669` has no reader in `.opencode`. P2 stands.\\n- **`iter5-P2-field-pass-through-untested`** (`.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/hooks/skill-advisor-cli-fallback-envelope.vitest.ts:49`) — re-read: the test's command-bearing case sends no `command`/`policy`/`ownerSkillId`, and the plugin tests assert none of the four fields. P2 stands.\\n\\nNo finding is a P0 or P1, so the verdict stays PASS with advisories.\\n\\n## Traceability Checks\\n\\n| Protocol | Level | Status | Notes |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| `spec_code` | core | pass | Every doc claim that changed in this area was checked against its code line; only the citations in finding 3 are wrong. |\\n| `checklist_evidence` | core | notApplicable | No checklist row governs this code pass. |\\n| `skill_agent` | overlay | notApplicable | No agent definition in this area. |\\n| `agent_cross_runtime` | overlay | pass | The six named runtimes resolve to the shared handler (claude/codex/cursor/devin/pi/dsh) or the plugin; both command-label paths carry the same fields. |\\n| `feature_catalog_code` | overlay | partial | The catalog leaf matches in substance; finding 3 is its citation drift. |\\n| `playbook_capability` | overlay | pass | The validation playbook's health-record sentence holds at every hook exit (see below). |\\n\\n## Integration Evidence\\n\\n- Hook exits that emit a health record: the kill-switch/prompt-gate branches (`user-prompt-submit.ts:302`, `:314`, `:330`), the delivered-brief branch (`:416`), the unhandled-exception branch (`:451`), and the fallback branch (`:514`). Each precedes its `return`, so every prompt path persists one record.\\n- Holdout hygiene counts: `command-prompts.jsonl` holds 176 rows and `holdout-prompts.jsonl` holds 66. No file in this area opens either fixture; no row text was read or printed in this lineage.\\n- The `.d.mts.map` artifacts are generated declaration maps; the four `yes` files were not read line by line, as recorded in iteration 5.\\n\\n## Edge Cases\\n\\n- **No new edge case.** The sweep found the same two removal residues and the same documentation offsets already recorded; nothing new was admitted.\\n- **Synthesis cycle.** Convergence at this iteration (no new findings, all four dimensions covered) means the next phase is synthesis, not a seventh iteration.\\n\\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\\n\\n- The child-session downgrade is still the only reader of `AI_SESSION_CHILD` in the advisor (`render.ts:529`); tests stub it in both golden files and the fallback envelope test, and the parity case compares it with `isChildSession`.\\n- The plugin's mapper and the hook fallback mapper agree on the four forwarded fields; the gap is test coverage, not behavior.\\n- The subprocess cap is the only bounded-output change in this area and both streams pass through it.\\n- The reader layer's containment is enforced before every read (iteration 3).\\n\\n## Ruled Out\\n\\n- **Any of the five open findings is a P0/P1.** Each is advisory: no data loss on a default path, no security boundary crossed, and each has a named concrete input. Verdict PASS.\\n- **The hook's health record misses a prompt path.** All six emit sites precede their returns, so skipped, delivered, fallback and exception paths all persist.\\n- **A seventh iteration would find something new.** The remaining unread artifacts are generated declaration maps and tests already read; the changed set is exhausted.\\n\\n## Next Focus\\n\\n- Dimension: synthesis\\n- Focus area: compile the lineage report from the registry and the six iterations; no further code review.\\n- Reason: convergence reached with all four dimensions covered and five active P2 advisories.\\n- Rotation status: all four dimensions complete.\\n- Blocked/productive carry-forward: none.\\n- Required evidence: the reducer-owned registry, the six iteration files and their deltas.\\n\\nReview verdict: PASS\\n\", \"path\": \"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/render-hooks-plugin-2/iterations/iteration-006.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794571701447,"end":1794571720935}}}}
